,"ja":["AIエージェント","プラグインアーキテクチャ","生産性ツール","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントのプラグインガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","플러그인 아키텍처","생산성 도구","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트 플러그인 가이드"],"es":["Agentes de IA","Guía de plugins","Productividad en flujos de trabajo","Cómo usar plugins en Agentes de IA","Alternativas a Agentes de IA","Instalación de plugins para Agentes de IA","Configuración de Agentes de IA","Mejora de la productividad con Agentes de IA"],"fr":["Agents IA","Guide des plugins","Productivité dans les flux de travail","Comment utiliser des plugins avec les Agents IA","Alternatives aux Agents IA","Installation de plugins pour les Agents IA","Configuration des Agents IA","Amélioration de la productivité avec les Agents IA"],"de":["KI-Agenten","Leitfaden für Plugins","Produktivitätssteigerung in Arbeitsabläufen","Wie man Plugins mit KI-Agenten verwendet","Alternativen zu KI-Agenten","Installation von Plugins für KI-Agenten","Konfiguration von KI-Agenten","Steigerung der Produktivität mit KI-Agenten"],"pt":["como usar agentes de IA","o que é agente de IA","guia de plugins para agentes de IA","alternativas para agentes de IA","agentes de IA vs assistentes virtuais","instalar agentes de IA","configurar agentes de IA","plugins para agentes de IA","desenvolvimento de agentes de IA"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое ИИ Агент","руководство по плагинам для ИИ Агентов","альтернативы для ИИ Агентов","ИИ Агенты vs виртуальные ассистенты","установка ИИ Агентов","настройка ИИ Агентов","плагины для ИИ Агентов","разработка ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","دليل الملحقات لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل المساعدين الافتراضيين","تثبيت عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","إعداد عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","ملحقات لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"kcosr","repo":"assistant","repoPath":"kcosr/assistant","stars":22,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T06:37:46Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"plugins-guide","description":"Best practices for working with plugins in the kcosr/assistant repository.","bodyPreview":"# Plugin Development Guide (General Best Practices)\n\nThis guide captures reusable patterns for building panel plugins: panel chrome, operations vs. WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, icons, CLI packaging, and cross‑platform behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Panel Header Chrome (Standard Controls)\n\n**All panels should render the standard chrome header** and let the shared `PanelChromeController` wire up controls. The header is built from three sections:\n\n1. **Main** (title + optional instance dropdown)\n2. **","body":"# Plugin Development Guide (General Best Practices)\n\nThis guide captures reusable patterns for building panel plugins: panel chrome, operations vs. WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, icons, CLI packaging, and cross‑platform behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Panel Header Chrome (Standard Controls)\n\n**All panels should render the standard chrome header** and let the shared `PanelChromeController` wire up controls. The header is built from three sections:\n\n1. **Main** (title + optional instance dropdown)\n2. **Plugin controls** (custom buttons)\n3. **Frame controls** (toggle/move/reorder/menu/close)\n\n### Required structure\n\n```html\n<div class=\"panel-header panel-chrome-row\" data-role=\"chrome-row\">\n  <div class=\"panel-header-main\">\n    <span class=\"panel-header-label\" data-role=\"chrome-title\">Panel Title</span>\n    <div class=\"panel-chrome-instance\" data-role=\"instance-actions\">\n      <!-- Instance dropdown markup here -->\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel-chrome-plugin-controls\" data-role=\"chrome-plugin-controls\">\n    <!-- plugin-specific buttons go here -->\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel-chrome-frame-controls\" data-role=\"chrome-controls\">\n    <!-- standard move/reorder/menu/close buttons -->\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Frame controls markup\n\nCopy the structure from existing panels like **notes** or **scheduled-sessions** (includes toggle, move, reorder, menu, close). The `PanelChromeController` attaches handlers based on `data-action` attributes.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PanelChromeController Responsibilities\n\nThe controller:\n- wires up frame controls\n- manages responsive layout\n- optionally wires up the instance dropdown\n\nYou must pass the instance dropdown container with:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"panel-chrome-instance-dropdown\" data-role=\"instance-dropdown-container\">…</div>\n```\n\nThen initialize:\n\n```ts\nchromeController = new PanelChromeController({\n  root: container,\n  host,\n  title: ''Panel Title'',\n  onInstanceChange: (instanceId) => {\n    selectedInstanceId = instanceId;\n    persistState();\n    void refreshList();\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Multi‑profile selection (shared profiles)\n\nInstance IDs now map to **shared profiles** declared at the top level `profiles` config.\nWhen you want multi‑profile selection in a panel, opt into it explicitly:\n\n```ts\nchromeController = new PanelChromeController({\n  root: container,\n  host,\n  title: ''Notes'',\n  instanceSelectionMode: ''multi'',\n  onInstanceChange: (instanceIds) => {\n    selectedInstanceIds = instanceIds;\n    activeInstanceId = instanceIds[0] ?? ''default'';\n    persistState();\n    void refreshList();\n  },\n});\n\nchromeController.setInstances(instances, selectedInstanceIds);\n```\n\n**Context:** include both the active instance and the full selection:\n\n```ts\nhost.setContext(contextKey, {\n  instance_id: activeInstanceId,\n  instance_ids: selectedInstanceIds,\n  contextAttributes: {\n    ''instance-id'': activeInstanceId,\n    ''instance-ids'': selectedInstanceIds.join('',''),\n  },\n});\n```\n\nNotes:\n- `default` is always available (implicit).\n- Non‑default instance ids must match a configured profile id.\n- Items still belong to a single instance/profile (edits happen in one profile).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Icons and Header Dock\n\nPanel icons shown in the **header dock** come from the **panel manifest**. The manifest `icon` value must match a key in `packages/web-client/src/utils/icons.ts`.\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n\"icon\": \"fileText\"\n```\n\nIf the icon name is invalid, the UI falls back to `panelGrid` (window/grid icon).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Operations vs WebSocket for CRUD\n\n### Recommended pattern\n\nUse **HTTP operations** for CRUD and **WebSocket events only for broadcast updates**:\n\n- `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete` → **HTTP operations**\n- real‑time updates → **WebSocket `panel_update`**\n\nThis avoids startup races when WebSocket isn’t ready yet (common on mobile).\n\n### Generic helper\n\n```ts\nasync function callOperation<T>(operation: string, body: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<T> {\n  const response = await apiFetch(`/api/plugins/<pluginId>/operations/${operation}`, {\n    method: ''POST'',\n    headers: { ''content-type'': ''application/json'' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  const payload = (await response.json()) as { ok: true; result: T } | { error: string };\n  if (!response.ok || ''error'' in payload) throw new Error(payload.error);\n  return payload.result;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Extra HTTP Routes for Binary Files\n\nOperations always return JSON. For binary endpoints (file download/preview), use **`extraHttpRoutes`** in the plugin module:\n\n```ts\nextraHttpRoutes: [\n  async (_context, req, res, url, segments) => {\n    if (req.method === ''GET'' && segments[3] === ''files'') {\n      res.setHeader(''Content-Disposition'', ''inline; filename=\"...\"'');\n      res.end(fileBuffer);\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  },\n]\n```\n\nThis is documented in `docs/PLUGIN_SDK.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. View vs Download Behavior\n\nWhen serving files, support both:\n\n- **View (inline)** — default\n- **Download (attachment)** — via query param (e.g. `?download=1`)\n\nThis enables an “open in browser” action and a “download” action with the same endpoint.\n\n---\n\n## 7. API Base URL\n\nWhen building URLs for fetch/open, use helpers in `web-client/src/utils/api.ts`:\n\n- `apiFetch()` for relative API calls\n- `getApiBaseUrl()` for full URLs when opening externally\n\nThis ensures URLs work in **Tauri**, **Capacitor**, and **web**.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Platform-Specific Open/Save\n\n### Web\n- `window.open(url, ''_blank'')` for view\n- `<a download>` for download\n\n### Tauri Desktop\n- **View:** `plugin:shell|open`\n- **Download:** native save dialog + backend command to write file\n\n### Capacitor Mobile\n- **View:** `@capacitor/browser`\n- **Download:** `@capacitor/filesystem` + optional `@capacitor/share`\n\n---\n\n## 9. Custom CLI Bundling\n\nPlugins can ship a custom CLI by placing `bin/cli.ts` in the plugin directory.\n\nBuild system compiles this file instead of auto‑generating a CLI from operations. Use this for:\n- reading files (`--file`)\n- custom args / processing\n- client-side behaviors before calling the API\n\n---\n\n## 9.1 Skill Bundle Export Controls\n\nBy default, `npm run build:plugins` exports skills to `dist/skills/<pluginId>/`.\nTo opt out for a specific plugin, set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skills\": { \"autoExport\": false }\n}\n```\n\nPassing `--skills <pluginId>` still forces export for that plugin.\n\nGenerated `SKILL.md` frontmatter includes `metadata.author` and `metadata.version`,\npopulated from the root `package.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Theme Variables\n\nUse shared theme variables:\n\n- `--color-text-primary`\n- `--color-text-secondary`\n- `--color-bg-hover`\n- `--color-bg-active`\n\nAvoid custom fallbacks like `--text-primary` or `prefers-color-scheme` blocks.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Shared Dialog Styling Duplication\n\nSome dialogs are rendered by shared web-client controllers but styled in multiple plugin bundles.\nFor example, list metadata dialog styles live in both:\n- `packages/plugins/official/lists/web/styles.css`\n- `packages/plugins/official/notes/web/styles.css`\n\nWhen adjusting `.list-metadata-*` rules (or similar shared dialog styles), update both files to keep\nLists and Notes consistent.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Panel Context for Chat Input\n\nPanels can provide context that is injected into user chat messages and shown in the\ncontext preview above the input. Use the panel context key and include selection data.\n\n### Required pattern\n\n```ts\nconst contextKey = getPanelContextKey(host.panelId());\nhost.setContext(contextKey, {\n  type: ''list'', // or ''artifacts'', ''note'', etc.\n  id: activeContainerId,\n  name: activeContainerName,\n  description: activeContainerDescription ?? '''',\n  selectedItemIds,\n  selectedItems, // [{ id, title }]\n  selectedItemCount: selectedItemIds.length,\n  contextAttributes: {\n    ''instance-id'': selectedInstanceId,\n    // add custom attributes like ''selected-text'' for text selections\n  },\n});\nservices.notifyContextAvailabilityChange();\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `type`, `id`, and `name` are used to build the `<context ... />` line in chat.\n- `selectedItemIds`/`selectedItems` populate selection context (e.g., list rows).\n- `contextAttributes` is a key/value bag for extra metadata (keys should be kebab-case).\n- Call `services.notifyContextAvailabilityChange()` after updates so the preview refreshes.\n- Listen for `assistant:clear-context-selection` if you support selection clearing.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Recommended Panel Lifecycle\n\nOn mount:\n- fetch instances via HTTP\n- fetch initial list via HTTP\n- subscribe to WebSocket updates\n\nOn visibility change:\n- refresh list via HTTP\n\n---\n\nThis guide is meant as a reusable checklist for future plugin work (operations + binary endpoints, panel chrome, icons, CLI, and cross‑platform behaviors).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T13:10:12.748Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing customized productivity workflow extensions through plugin architecture.","zh":"适合需要通过插件架构进行定制化生产力工作流扩展的AI代理。","ja":"カスタマイズされた生産性ワークフロー拡張をプラグインアーキテクチャを介して必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"플러그인 아키텍처를 통해 사용자 지정 생산성 워크플로 확장을 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan extensiones de flujo de trabajo de productividad personalizadas a través de la arquitectura de plugins.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin d''extensions de flux de travail de productivité personnalisées via l''architecture de plugins.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die benutzerdefinierte Produktivitäts-Workflows durch Plugin-Architektur benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam de extensões de fluxo de trabalho de produtividade personalizadas por meio de arquitetura de plugin.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым требуются настраиваемые расширения рабочего процесса продуктивности через архитектуру плагинов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى امتدادات سير عمل إنتاجية مخصصة من خلال هندسة البرامج المضيفة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to integrate with panel-based personal assistants, utilizing WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, and custom plugins, while supporting Claude Code, Codex, and pi CLI agents with text and voice interfaces.","zh":"赋予代理集成面板式个人助手的能力，利用WebSocket使用，二进制端点和自定义插件，同时支持Claude Code，Codex和pi CLI代理的文本和语音接口。","ja":"エージェントにパネルベースのパーソナルアシスタントと統合する能力を与え、WebSocketの使用、バイナリエンドポイント、カスタムプラグインを利用し、Claude Code、Codex、pi CLIエージェントのテキストと音声インターフェイスをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트에 패널 기반 개인 조수와 통합할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며 WebSocket 사용, 바이너리 엔드 포인트 및 사용자 지정 플러그인을 활용하며 Claude Code, Codex 및 pi CLI 에이전트의 텍스트 및 음성 인터페이스를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a integrarse con asistentes personales basados en paneles, utilizando el uso de WebSocket, puntos finales binarios y plugins personalizados, mientras admite a los agentes Claude Code, Codex y pi CLI con interfaces de texto y voz.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''intégrer avec des assistants personnels basés sur des panneaux, en utilisant l''utilisation de WebSocket, des points de terminaison binaires et des plugins personnalisés, tout en prenant en charge les agents Claude Code, Codex et pi CLI avec des interfaces texte et voix.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, sich mit panelbasierten persönlichen Assistenten zu integrieren, indem sie WebSocket-Nutzung, Binär-Endpunkte und benutzerdefinierte Plugins verwenden, während sie Claude Code-, Codex- und pi-CLI-Agents mit Text- und Sprachinterfaces unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se integrarem com assistentes pessoais baseados em painéis, utilizando o uso de WebSocket, endpoints binários e plugins personalizados, além de dar suporte a agentes Claude Code, Codex e pi CLI com interfaces de texto e voz.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью интегрироваться с панельными личными помощниками, используя WebSocket, бинарные конечные точки и пользовательские плагины, а также поддерживает агентов Claude Code, Codex и pi CLI с текстовыми и голосовыми интерфейсами.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على الاندماج مع المساعدين الشخصيين القائمين على اللوحات، باستخدام استخدام WebSocket، ونقاط النهاية الثنائية، والبرامج المضيفة المخصصة، بالإضافة إلى دعم وكلاء Claude Code، Codex، و pi CLI مع واجهات النص والصوت."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing custom panel plugins for enhanced productivity","Integrating AI agents with panel-based workspaces","Extending workflow capabilities with cross-platform plugins"],"zh":["为增强生产力而开发自定义面板插件","将AI代理集成到面板式工作空间中","通过跨平台插件扩展工作流功能"],"ja":["生産性を高めるためのカスタムパネルプラグインの開発","AIエージェントをパネルベースのワークスペースに統合する","クロスプラットフォームプラグインを使用してワークフローの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["생산성을 향상시키기 위한 사용자 지정 패널 플러그인 개발","AI 에이전트를 패널 기반 워크스페이스와 통합","크로스 플랫폼 플러그인을 사용하여 워크플로우 기능 확장"],"es":["Desarrollar plugins de panel personalizados para una mayor productividad","Integrar agentes de IA con espacios de trabajo basados en paneles","Ampliar las capacidades de flujo de trabajo con plugins multiplataforma"],"fr":["Développer des plugins de panneau personnalisés pour une productivité améliorée","Intégrer des agents IA avec des espaces de travail basés sur des panneaux","Étendre les capacités de flux de travail avec des plugins multiplateforme"],"de":["Entwickeln von benutzerdefinierten Panel-Plugins für erhöhte Produktivität","Integrieren von KI-Agents in panelbasierte Arbeitsbereiche","Erweitern von Workflow-Fähigkeiten mit Cross-Platform-Plugins"],"pt":["Desenvolver plugins de painel personalizados para produtividade aprimorada","Integrar agentes de IA com ambientes de trabalho baseados em painéis","Estender capacidades de fluxo de trabalho com plugins cross-plataforma"],"ru":["Разработка пользовательских плагинов панели для повышения производительности","Интеграция агентов ИИ с панельными рабочими пространствами","Расширение возможностей рабочего процесса с помощью кроссплатформенных плагинов"],"ar":["تطوير برامج مضيفة مخصصة للوحة لتحسين الإنتاجية","دمج عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مع بيئات العمل القائمة على اللوحات","توسيع قدرات سير العمل باستخدام برامج مضيفة متعددة المنصات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of plugin development best practices","Limited to agents compatible with Claude Code, Codex, and pi CLI"],"zh":["需要了解插件开发的最佳实践","仅限与Claude Code，Codex和pi CLI兼容的代理"],"ja":["プラグイン開発のベストプラクティスの知識が必要","Claude Code、Codex、pi CLIと互換性のあるエージェントのみに限定される"],"ko":["플러그인 개발 최고 실천 방법에 대한 지식이 필요","Claude Code, Codex 및 pi CLI와 호환되는 에이전트에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las mejores prácticas de desarrollo de plugins","Limitado a agentes compatibles con Claude Code, Codex y pi CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances sur les meilleures pratiques de développement de plugins","Limité aux agents compatibles avec Claude Code, Codex et pi CLI"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse über Best Practices für die Entwicklung von Plugins","Begrenzt auf Agents, die mit Claude Code, Codex und pi CLI kompatibel sind"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de práticas recomendadas de desenvolvimento de plugins","Limitado a agentes compatíveis com Claude Code, Codex e pi CLI"],"ru":["Требует знания лучших практик разработки плагинов","Ограничен агентами, совместимыми с Claude Code, Codex и pi CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة أفضل الممارسات لتطوير البرامج المضيفة","محدود بالوكلاء المتوافقة مع Claude Code، Codex و pi CLI"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"693e688f634c6a92ec1e2d867dd752cd2b08fab3c6453e18bef72acf14fecb94","qualityScore":47}');
