"멀티 프로젝트 워크플ロー 관리 지원","장기 실행 태스크 관리","인간-AI 협력 기능","CLI 인터페이스","Git Worktree 통합","PySide6 지원"],"es":["Gestión de contexto y enfoque","Trabajo paralelo y colaboración humana-AI","Integración con CLI y Git","Soporte para proyectos de desarrollo multi-proyecto","Herramientas de productividad para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Gestion du contexte et de la focalisation","Travail parallèle et collaboration humaine-AI","Intégration avec CLI et Git","Prise en charge des projets de développement multi-projet","Outils de productivité pour les développeurs"],"de":["Kontext- und Fokusverwaltung","Parallelarbeit und menschliche KI-Kollaboration","Integration mit CLI und Git","Unterstützung für Entwicklungsprojekte mit mehreren Projekten","Produktivitätstools für Entwickler"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de contexto e foco em desenvolvimento assistido por IA","Suporte a fluxos de trabalho multi-projeto","Integração com Git Worktree","Interface de linha de comando (CLI)","Compatibilidade com PySide6"],"ru":["Управление контекстом и фокусом в разработке с помощью ИИ","Поддержка многопроектных рабочих процессов","Интеграция с Git Worktree","Интерфейс командной строки (CLI)","Совместимость с PySide6"],"ar":["إدارة السياق والتركيز في التطوير بمساعدة الإجابة الذكية","دعم سير عمل متعدد المشاريع","التكامل مع Git Worktree","واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI)","التوافق مع PySide6"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能体","openspec-explore","开发者工具","CLI","Git Worktree","PySide6","如何使用openspec-explore","openspec-explore安装","openspec-explore设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","openspec-explore","開発者ツール","CLI","Git Worktree","PySide6","openspec-exploreの使い方","openspec-exploreのインストール","openspec-exploreのセットアップガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","openspec-explore","개발자 도구","CLI","Git Worktree","PySide6","openspec-explore 사용법","openspec-explore 설치","openspec-explore 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar Agente de IA","qué es Agente de IA","herramientas de desarrollo de IA","alternativas a openspec-explore","openspec-explore vs otros agentes de IA","instalación de openspec-explore","guía de configuración de openspec-explore"],"fr":["comment utiliser un Agent IA","quoi est un Agent IA","outils de développement d''IA","alternatives à openspec-explore","openspec-explore vs d''autres agents d''IA","installation d''openspec-explore","guide de configuration d''openspec-explore"],"de":["wie man AI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein AI-Agent","Entwicklertools für KI","Alternativen zu openspec-explore","openspec-explore vs andere KI-Agents","Installation von openspec-explore","Konfigurationsanleitung für openspec-explore"],"pt":["ferramentas de agente de IA","desenvolvimento assistido por IA","gerenciamento de contexto","fluxos de trabalho multi-projeto","Git Worktree","CLI","PySide6","como usar openspec-explore","o que é openspec-explore"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","разработка с помощью ИИ","управление контекстом","многопроектные рабочие процессы","Git Worktree","CLI","PySide6","как использовать openspec-explore","что такое openspec-explore"],"ar":["أدوات الإجابة الذكية","التطوير بمساعدة الإجابة الذكية","إدارة السياق","سير عمل متعدد المشاريع","Git Worktree","CLI","PySide6","كيفية استخدام openspec-explore","ما هي openspec-explore"]}},"owner":"tatargabor","repo":"wt-tools","repoPath":"tatargabor/wt-tools","stars":9,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T01:28:20Z","topics":["ai-agent","claude-code","cli","developer-tools","git-worktree","mcp","pyside6"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-explore","description":"Enter explore mode - a thinking partner for exploring ideas, investigating problems, and clarifying requirements. Use when the user wants to think through something before or during a change.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s c","body":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s capturing thinking, not implementing.\n\n**This is a stance, not a workflow.** There are no fixed steps, no required sequence, no mandatory outputs. You''re a thinking partner helping the user explore.\n\n---\n\n## The Stance\n\n- **Curious, not prescriptive** - Ask questions that emerge naturally, don''t follow a script\n- **Open threads, not interrogations** - Surface multiple interesting directions and let the user follow what resonates. Don''t funnel them through a single path of questions.\n- **Visual** - Use ASCII diagrams liberally when they''d help clarify thinking\n- **Adaptive** - Follow interesting threads, pivot when new information emerges\n- **Patient** - Don''t rush to conclusions, let the shape of the problem emerge\n- **Grounded** - Explore the actual codebase when relevant, don''t just theorize\n\n---\n\n## What You Might Do\n\nDepending on what the user brings, you might:\n\n**Explore the problem space**\n- Ask clarifying questions that emerge from what they said\n- Challenge assumptions\n- Reframe the problem\n- Find analogies\n\n**Investigate the codebase**\n- Map existing architecture relevant to the discussion\n- Find integration points\n- Identify patterns already in use\n- Surface hidden complexity\n\n**Compare options**\n- Brainstorm multiple approaches\n- Build comparison tables\n- Sketch tradeoffs\n- Recommend a path (if asked)\n\n**Visualize**\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│     Use ASCII diagrams liberally        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                         │\n│   ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        │\n│   │ State  │────────▶│ State  │        │\n│   │   A    │         │   B    │        │\n│   └────────┘         └────────┘        │\n│                                         │\n│   System diagrams, state machines,      │\n│   data flows, architecture sketches,    │\n│   dependency graphs, comparison tables  │\n│                                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Surface risks and unknowns**\n- Identify what could go wrong\n- Find gaps in understanding\n- Suggest spikes or investigations\n\n---\n\n## OpenSpec Awareness\n\nYou have full context of the OpenSpec system. Use it naturally, don''t force it.\n\n### Check memory first\n\nBefore exploring independently, check injected memory context from `<system-reminder>` tags. Summarize what you already know from memory, then fill in gaps with codebase exploration.\n\n### Check for context\n\nAt the start, quickly check what exists:\n```bash\nopenspec list --json\n```\n\nThis tells you:\n- If there are active changes\n- Their names, schemas, and status\n- What the user might be working on\n\n### When no change exists\n\nThink freely. When insights crystallize, you might offer:\n\n- \"This feels solid enough to start a change. Want me to create one?\"\n  → Can transition to `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`\n- Or keep exploring - no pressure to formalize\n\n### When a change exists\n\nIf the user mentions a change or you detect one is relevant:\n\n1. **Read existing artifacts for context**\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`\n   - etc.\n\n2. **Reference them naturally in conversation**\n   - \"Your design mentions using Redis, but we just realized SQLite fits better...\"\n   - \"The proposal scopes this to premium users, but we''re now thinking everyone...\"\n\n3. **Offer to capture when decisions are made**\n\n   | Insight Type | Where to Capture |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | New requirement discovered | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Requirement changed | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Design decision made | `design.md` |\n   | Scope changed | `proposal.md` |\n   | New work identified | `tasks.md` |\n   | Assumption invalidated | Relevant artifact |\n\n   Example offers:\n   - \"That''s a design decision. Capture it in design.md?\"\n   - \"This is a new requirement. Add it to specs?\"\n   - \"This changes scope. Update the proposal?\"\n\n4. **The user decides** - Offer and move on. Don''t pressure. Don''t auto-capture.\n\n---\n\n## What You Don''t Have To Do\n\n- Follow a script\n- Ask the same questions every time\n- Produce a specific artifact\n- Reach a conclusion\n- Stay on topic if a tangent is valuable\n- Be brief (this is thinking time)\n\n---\n\n## Handling Different Entry Points\n\n**User brings a vague idea:**\n```\nUser: I''m thinking about adding real-time collaboration\n\nYou: Real-time collab is a big space. Let me think about this...\n\n      COLLABORATION SPECTRUM\n      ════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n      Awareness          Coordination         Sync\n          │                   │                 │\n          ▼                   ▼                 ▼\n      ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        ┌────────┐\n      │Presence│         │Cursors │        │  CRDT  │\n      │  \"3    │         │ Multi  │        │Conflict│\n      │online\" │         │ select │        │  free  │\n      └────────┘         └────────┘        └────────┘\n          │                   │                 │\n       trivial            moderate           complex\n\n      Where''s your head at?\n```\n\n**User brings a specific problem:**\n```\nUser: The auth system is a mess\n\nYou: [reads codebase]\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │              CURRENT AUTH FLOW              │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                        │\n          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n          ▼             ▼             ▼\n     ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐\n     │ Google  │  │  GitHub │  │  Email  │\n     │  OAuth  │  │  OAuth  │  │  Magic  │\n     └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘\n          │             │             │\n          └─────────────┼─────────────┘\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │  Session  │\n                  └─────┬─────┘\n                        │\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │   Perms   │\n                  └───────────┘\n\n     I see three tangles. Which one''s burning?\n```\n\n**User is stuck mid-implementation:**\n```\nUser: /opsx:explore add-auth-system\n      The OAuth integration is more complex than expected\n\nYou: [reads change artifacts]\n\n     You''re on task 4: \"Implement OAuth flow\"\n\n     Let me trace what''s involved...\n\n     [draws diagram, explores options, suggests paths]\n\n     Want to update the design to reflect this?\n     Or add a spike task to investigate?\n```\n\n**User wants to compare options:**\n```\nUser: Should we use Postgres or SQLite?\n\nYou: Generic answer is boring. What''s the context?\n\nUser: A CLI tool that tracks local dev environments\n\nYou: That changes everything.\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │         CLI TOOL DATA STORAGE                  │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n     Key constraints:\n     • No daemon running\n     • Must work offline\n     • Single user\n\n                  SQLite          Postgres\n     Deployment   embedded ✓      needs server ✗\n     Offline      yes ✓           no ✗\n     Single file  yes ✓           no ✗\n\n     SQLite. Not even close.\n\n     Unless... is there a sync component?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Ending Discovery\n\nThere''s no required ending. Discovery might:\n\n- **Flow into action**: \"Ready to start? /opsx:new or /opsx:ff\"\n- **Result in artifact updates**: \"Updated design.md with these decisions\"\n- **Just provide clarity**: User has what they need, moves on\n- **Continue later**: \"We can pick this up anytime\"\n\nWhen it feels like things are crystallizing, you might summarize:\n\n```\n## What We Figured Out\n\n**The problem**: [crystallized understanding]\n\n**The approach**: [if one emerged]\n\n**Open questions**: [if any remain]\n\n**Next steps** (if ready):\n- Create a change: /opsx:new <name>\n- Fast-forward to tasks: /opsx:ff <name>\n- Keep exploring: just keep talking\n```\n\nBut this summary is optional. Sometimes the thinking IS the value.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Don''t implement** - Never write code or implement features. Creating OpenSpec artifacts is fine, writing application code is not.\n- **Don''t fake understanding** - If something is unclear, dig deeper\n- **Don''t rush** - Discovery is thinking time, not task time\n- **Don''t force structure** - Let patterns emerge naturally\n- **Don''t auto-capture** - Offer to save insights, don''t just do it\n- **Do visualize** - A good diagram is worth many paragraphs\n- **Do explore the codebase** - Ground discussions in reality\n- **Do question assumptions** - Including the user''s and your own\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T01:54:05.823Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced context management and human-AI collaboration in multi-project workflows.","zh":"适合需要高级上下文管理和人工智能协作的多项目工作流的AI代理。","ja":"高度なコンテキスト管理と人間とAIのコラボレーションが必要なマルチプロジェクトワークフロー用のAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 컨텍스트 관리 및 인간-AI 협업이 필요한 다중 프로젝트 워크플로를 위한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que requieren una gestión avanzada de contexto y colaboración humano-IA en flujos de trabajo multi-proyecto.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant une gestion avancée du contexte et une collaboration humain-IA dans des flux de travail multi-projets.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die eine erweiterte Kontextverwaltung und eine Mensch-KI-Zusammenarbeit in Multi-Projekt-Workflows erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que requerem gerenciamento avançado de contexto e colaboração humano-IA em fluxos de trabalho multi-projeto.","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, требующих передового управления контекстом и сотрудничества человека и ИИ в многопроектных рабочих процессах.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يتطلبون إدارة متقدمة للسياق والتعاون بين البشر والذكاء الاصطناعي في سير العمل متعددة المشاريع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage context, focus, and parallel work using OpenSpec artifacts, enabling seamless human-AI collaboration and efficient long-running task management through protocols like file reading and code searching, while strictly separating thinking from implementation.","zh":"通过OpenSpec工件，赋予代理管理上下文、焦点和并行工作的能力，实现无缝的人类-AI协作和通过协议（如文件读取和代码搜索）高效的长期任务管理，同时严格分离思考和实现。","ja":"OpenSpecアーティファクトを使用して、コンテキスト、フォーカス、および並列作業を管理するエージェントの能力を付与し、シームレスな人間とAIのコラボレーションと、ファイルの読み取りやコードの検索などのプロトコルを介した効率的な長時間のタスク管理を可能にし、思考と実装を厳密に分離します。","ko":"OpenSpec 아티팩트를 사용하여 컨텍스트, 포커스 및 병렬 작업을 관리하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하여 인간-AI 협업과 파일 읽기 및 코드 검색 등의 프로토콜을 통해 효율적인 장기 작업 관리를 가능하게 하며, 사고와 구현을 엄격하게 분리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar el contexto, el enfoque y el trabajo paralelo utilizando artefactos OpenSpec, lo que permite una colaboración humana-IA sin problemas y una gestión eficiente de tareas de ejecución prolongada a través de protocolos como la lectura de archivos y la búsqueda de código, al tiempo que separa estrictamente el pensamiento de la implementación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer le contexte, la concentration et le travail parallèle en utilisant des artefacts OpenSpec, ce qui permet une collaboration humain-IA sans accroc et une gestion efficace des tâches à long terme via des protocoles tels que la lecture de fichiers et la recherche de code, tout en séparant strictement la réflexion de la mise en œuvre.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Kontext, Fokus und parallele Arbeit mit OpenSpec-Artefakten zu verwalten, was eine nahtlose Mensch-KI-Zusammenarbeit und eine effiziente Verwaltung von Langzeit-Aufgaben durch Protokolle wie Dateilesen und Codesuche ermöglicht, während es streng zwischen Denken und Implementierung trennt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar contexto, foco e trabalho paralelo usando artefatos OpenSpec, permitindo uma colaboração humana-IA sem interrupções e uma gestão eficiente de tarefas de longa duração por meio de protocolos como leitura de arquivos e busca de código, enquanto separa estritamente o pensamento da implementação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять контекстом, сосредоточением и параллельной работой с помощью артефактов OpenSpec, обеспечивая беспрепятственное сотрудничество человека и ИИ и эффективное управление задачами длительного выполнения по протоколам, таким как чтение файлов и поиск кода, при этом строго разделяя мыслительную и реализационную фазы.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة السياق والتركيز والعمل المتوازي باستخدام مكونات OpenSpec، مما يُمكّن من تعاون سلس بين البشر والذكاء الاصطناعي وإدارة فعالة للمهام الطويلة المدى من خلال بروتوكولات مثل قراءة الملفات و البحث عن الكود، مع فصل صارم بين مرحلتي التفكير والتنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Entering explore mode for deep thinking and visualization","Creating OpenSpec proposals and designs for collaborative projects","Investigating codebases for informed decision-making"],"zh":["进入探索模式进行深入思考和可视化","创建OpenSpec提案和设计用于协作项目","调查代码库以进行明智的决策"],"ja":["深い思考と視覚化のための探索モードに入る","コラボレーションプロジェクト用のOpenSpec提案と設計を作成する","情報に基づいた意思決定のためのコードベースを調査する"],"ko":["깊은思考과 시각화를 위한 탐색 모드に入る","협력 프로젝트를 위한 OpenSpec 제안 및 디자인を作成한다","정보에 기반한 의사 결정을 위한 코드베이스를 조사한다"],"es":["Entrar en modo de exploración para una reflexión profunda y visualización","Crear propuestas y diseños OpenSpec para proyectos colaborativos","Investigar códigos fuente para la toma de decisiones informadas"],"fr":["Entrer en mode d''exploration pour une réflexion approfondie et une visualisation","Créer des propositions et des conceptions OpenSpec pour des projets collaboratifs","Investiguer des bases de code pour une prise de décision éclairée"],"de":["Explorationsmodus für tiefes Nachdenken und Visualisierung betreten","Erstellen von OpenSpec-Vorschlägen und -Entwürfen für kollaborative Projekte","Untersuchen von Codebasen für eine fundierte Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Entrar no modo de exploração para pensamento profundo e visualização","Criar propostas e designs OpenSpec para projetos colaborativos","Investigar código-fonte para tomada de decisões informadas"],"ru":["Вход в режим исследования для глубокого мышления и визуализации","Создание предложений и дизайнов OpenSpec для совместных проектов","Изучение кодовой базы для принятия обоснованных решений"],"ar":["الدخول إلى وضع الاستكشاف للتفكير العميق والتصوير","إنشاء مقترحات وتصاميم OpenSpec لمشاريع تعاونية","التحقيق في قاعدة الكود لاتخاذ قرارات مدروسة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Must not write code or implement features in explore mode","Requires strict separation of thinking and implementation phases"],"zh":["探索模式下不得编写代码或实现功能","需要严格分离思考和实现阶段"],"ja":["探索モードではコードを書いたり機能を実装したりしてはならない","思考と実装の段階を厳密に分離する必要がある"],"ko":["탐색 모드에서는 코드를 작성하거나 기능을 구현할 수 없다","사고와 구현 단계를 엄격하게 분리해야 한다"],"es":["No debe escribir código ni implementar características en modo de exploración","Requiere una separación estricta de las fases de pensamiento e implementación"],"fr":["Ne doit pas écrire de code ou mettre en œuvre des fonctionnalités en mode d''exploration","Exige une séparation stricte des phases de réflexion et de mise en œuvre"],"de":["Darf in Explorationsmodus keinen Code schreiben oder Funktionen implementieren","Erfordert eine strenge Trennung der Denk- und Implementierungsphasen"],"pt":["Não deve escrever código ou implementar recursos no modo de exploração","Exige separação estrita das fases de pensamento e implementação"],"ru":["Не должен писать код или реализовывать функции в режиме исследования","Требует строгого разделения фаз мышления и реализации"],"ar":["لا يجب书ه الكود أو تنفيذ الميزات في وضع الاستكشاف","يتطلب فصلًا صارمًا بين مرحلتي التفكير والتنفيذ"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"1529ae4e8f63033aee2d94a71045667e2c3280ff9f0283421523520ccc1aef47","qualityScore":47}');
