r la gestión","Compatibilidad con harvester y k8s-at-home"],"fr":["Intégration avec Kubernetes","Prise en charge de Rancher","Outils DevOps pour améliorer l''efficacité","Dépôt mono pour simplifier la gestion","Compatibilité avec harvester et k8s-at-home"],"de":["Integration mit Kubernetes","Unterstützung für Rancher","DevOps-Tools für verbesserte Effizienz","Mono-Repository für vereinfachte Verwaltung","Kompatibilität mit harvester und k8s-at-home"],"pt":["Otimização de infraestrutura com Kubernetes","Gerenciamento de cluster com Rancher","Integração com Harvester","Suporte a k8s-at-home","Implantação com RKE","Desenvolvimento de aplicações com DevOps"],"ru":["Оптимизация инфраструктуры с помощью Kubernetes","Управление кластером с помощью Rancher","Интеграция с Harvester","Поддержка k8s-at-home","Развертывание с помощью RKE","Разработка приложений с помощью DevOps"],"ar":["تحسين البنية التحتية مع Kubernetes","إدارة المجموعة مع Rancher","التكامل مع Harvester","دعم k8s-at-home","تثبيت مع RKE","تطوير التطبيقات مع DevOps"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SRE AIエージェント","DevOps工具","Kubernetes","Rancher","Harvester","系统可靠性工程","如何使用SRE AIエージェント","SRE AIエージェント安装","SRE AIエージェント设置指南"],"ja":["SRE AIエージェント","DevOpsツール","Kubernetes","Rancher","Harvester","システムの信頼性エンジニアリング","SRE AIエージェントの使用方法","SRE AIエージェントのインストール","SRE AIエージェントの設定ガイド"],"ko":["SRE AI 에이전트","DevOps 도구","Kubernetes","Rancher","Harvester","시스템 안정성 엔지니어링","SRE AI 에이전트 사용법","SRE AI 에이전트 설치","SRE AI 에이전트 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de SRE","DevOps","Kubernetes","Rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","cómo usar SRE","qué es SRE","alternativas a SRE","guía de instalación de SRE"],"fr":["outils SRE","DevOps","Kubernetes","Rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","comment utiliser SRE","quoi est SRE","alternatives à SRE","guide d''installation SRE"],"de":["SRE-Tools","DevOps","Kubernetes","Rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","wie man SRE verwendet","was ist SRE","Alternativen zu SRE","Installationsanleitung für SRE"],"pt":["o que é sre","ferramentas de sre","otimização de infraestrutura","kubernetes","rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","rke","devops","como usar sre"],"ru":["что такое sre","инструменты sre","оптимизация инфраструктуры","kubernetes","rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","rke","devops","как использовать sre"],"ar":["ما هو sre","أدوات sre","تحسين البنية التحتية","kubernetes","rancher","harvester","k8s-at-home","rke","devops","كيفية استخدام sre"]}},"owner":"ionfury","repo":"homelab","repoPath":"ionfury/homelab","stars":22,"forks":3,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T17:35:15Z","topics":["devops","harvester","k8s-at-home","kubernetes","rancher","rke"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sre","description":"|","bodyPreview":"> **Cluster access, KUBECONFIG patterns, and internal service URLs** are in the `k8s` skill.\n\n# Debugging Kubernetes Incidents\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **5 Whys Analysis** - NEVER stop at symptoms. Ask \"why\" until you reach the root cause.\n- **Read-Only Investigation** - Observe and analyze, never modify resources on integration/live. Dev cluster permits direct mutations for debugging (see troubleshooter agent boundaries)\n- **Multi-Source Correlation** - Combine logs, events, metrics for complete","body":"> **Cluster access, KUBECONFIG patterns, and internal service URLs** are in the `k8s` skill.\n\n# Debugging Kubernetes Incidents\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **5 Whys Analysis** - NEVER stop at symptoms. Ask \"why\" until you reach the root cause.\n- **Read-Only Investigation** - Observe and analyze, never modify resources on integration/live. Dev cluster permits direct mutations for debugging (see troubleshooter agent boundaries)\n- **Multi-Source Correlation** - Combine logs, events, metrics for complete picture\n- **Research Unknown Services** - Check documentation before deep investigation\n- **Zero Alert Tolerance** - Every firing alert must be addressed immediately: fix the root cause, or as a last resort, create a declarative Silence CR with justification. Never ignore, defer, or dismiss a firing alert.\n\n## The 5 Whys Analysis (CRITICAL)\n\n**You MUST apply 5 Whys before concluding any investigation.** Stopping at symptoms leads to ineffective fixes.\n\n### How to Apply\n\n1. Start with the observed symptom\n2. Ask \"Why did this happen?\" for each answer\n3. Continue until you reach an actionable root cause (typically 5 levels)\n\n### Example\n\n```\nSymptom: Helm install failed with \"context deadline exceeded\"\n\nWhy #1: Why did Helm timeout?\n  → Pods never became Ready\n\nWhy #2: Why weren''t pods Ready?\n  → Pods stuck in Pending state\n\nWhy #3: Why were pods Pending?\n  → PVCs couldn''t bind (StorageClass \"fast\" not found)\n\nWhy #4: Why was StorageClass missing?\n  → longhorn-storage Kustomization failed to apply\n\nWhy #5: Why did the Kustomization fail?\n  → numberOfReplicas was integer instead of string\n\nROOT CAUSE: YAML type coercion issue\nFIX: Use properly typed variable for StorageClass parameters\n```\n\n### Red Flags You Haven''t Reached Root Cause\n\n- Your \"fix\" is increasing a timeout or retry count\n- Your \"fix\" addresses the symptom, not what caused it\n- You can still ask \"but why did THAT happen?\"\n- Multiple issues share the same underlying cause\n\n```\nBAD:  \"Helm timed out → increase timeout to 15m\"\nGOOD: \"Helm timed out → ... → Kustomization type error → fix YAML\"\n```\n\n## Investigation Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Triage\n\n1. **Confirm cluster** - Ask user: \"Which cluster? (dev/integration/live)\"\n2. **Assess severity** - P1 (down) / P2 (degraded) / P3 (minor) / P4 (cosmetic)\n3. **Identify scope** - Pod / Deployment / Namespace / Cluster-wide\n\n### Phase 2: Data Collection\n\n```bash\n# Pod status and events\nkubectl get pods -n <namespace>\nkubectl describe pod <pod> -n <namespace>\n\n# Logs (current and previous)\nkubectl logs <pod> -n <namespace> --tail=100\nkubectl logs <pod> -n <namespace> --previous\n\n# Events timeline\nkubectl get events -n <namespace> --sort-by=''.lastTimestamp''\n\n# Resource usage\nkubectl top pods -n <namespace>\n```\n\n**Metrics and alerts via kubectl exec (Prometheus is behind OAuth2 Proxy — DNS URLs won''t work for API queries):**\n\n```bash\n# Check firing alerts\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl exec -n monitoring prometheus-kube-prometheus-stack-0 -c prometheus -- \\\n  wget -qO- ''http://localhost:9090/api/v1/alerts'' | jq ''.data.alerts[] | select(.state == \"firing\")''\n\n# Pod restart metrics\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl exec -n monitoring prometheus-kube-prometheus-stack-0 -c prometheus -- \\\n  wget -qO- ''http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total[1h])>0'' | jq ''.data.result''\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Correlation\n\n1. Extract timestamps from logs, events, metrics\n2. Identify what happened FIRST (root cause)\n3. Trace the cascade of effects\n\n### Phase 4: Root Cause (5 Whys)\n\nApply 5 Whys analysis. Validate:\n- **Temporal**: Did it happen BEFORE the symptom?\n- **Causal**: Does it logically explain the symptom?\n- **Evidence**: Is there supporting data?\n- **Complete**: Have you asked \"why\" enough times?\n\n### Phase 5: Remediation\n\nUse **AskUserQuestion** tool to present fix options when multiple valid approaches exist.\n\nProvide recommendations only (read-only investigation):\n- **Immediate**: Rollback, scale, restart\n- **Permanent**: Code/config fixes\n- **Prevention**: Alerts, quotas, tests\n\n## Quick Diagnosis\n\n| Symptom | First Check | Common Cause |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|\n| `ImagePullBackOff` | `describe pod` events | Wrong image/registry auth |\n| `Pending` | Events, node capacity | Insufficient resources |\n| `CrashLoopBackOff` | `logs --previous` | App error, missing config |\n| `OOMKilled` | Memory limits | Memory leak, limits too low |\n| `Unhealthy` | Probe config | Slow startup, wrong endpoint |\n| Service unreachable | Hubble dropped traffic | **Network policy blocking** |\n| Can''t reach database | Hubble + namespace labels | Missing access label |\n| Gateway returns 503 | Hubble from istio-gateway | Missing profile label |\n\n## Common Failure Chains\n\n**Storage failures cascade:**\n```\nStorageClass missing → PVC Pending → Pod Pending → Helm timeout\n```\n\n**Network failures cascade:**\n```\nDNS failure → Service unreachable → Health check fails → Pod restarted\n```\n\n**Network policy failures cascade:**\n```\nMissing namespace profile label → No ingress allowed → Service unreachable from gateway\nMissing access label → Can''t reach database → App fails health checks → CrashLoopBackOff\n```\n\n**Secret failures cascade:**\n```\nExternalSecret fails → Secret missing → Pod CrashLoopBackOff\n```\n\n## Network Policy Debugging (Cilium + Hubble)\n\n**Network policies are ENFORCED - all traffic is implicitly denied unless allowed.**\n\n### Check for Blocked Traffic\n\n```bash\n# Setup Hubble access (run once per session)\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl port-forward -n kube-system svc/hubble-relay 4245:80 &\n\n# See dropped traffic in a namespace\nhubble observe --verdict DROPPED --namespace <namespace> --since 5m\n\n# See what''s trying to reach a service\nhubble observe --to-namespace <namespace> --verdict DROPPED --since 5m\n\n# Check specific traffic flow\nhubble observe --from-namespace <source> --to-namespace <dest> --since 5m\n```\n\n### Common Network Policy Issues\n\n| Symptom | Check | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| Service unreachable from gateway | `kubectl get ns <ns> --show-labels` | Add profile label |\n| Can''t reach database | Check `access.network-policy.homelab/postgres` label | Add access label |\n| Pods can''t resolve DNS | Hubble DNS drops (rare - baseline allows) | Check for custom egress blocking |\n| Inter-pod communication fails | Hubble intra-namespace drops | Baseline should allow - check for overrides |\n\n### Namespace Labels Checklist\n\n```bash\n# Check namespace has required labels\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl get ns <namespace> -o jsonpath=''{.metadata.labels}'' | jq\n\n# Required for app namespaces:\n# - network-policy.homelab/profile: standard|internal|internal-egress|isolated\n\n# Optional access labels:\n# - access.network-policy.homelab/postgres: \"true\"\n# - access.network-policy.homelab/garage-s3: \"true\"\n# - access.network-policy.homelab/kube-api: \"true\"\n```\n\n### Emergency: Disable Network Policies\n\n```bash\n# Escape hatch - disables enforcement for namespace (triggers alert after 5m)\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl label namespace <ns> network-policy.homelab/enforcement=disabled\n\n# Re-enable after fixing\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl label namespace <ns> network-policy.homelab/enforcement-\n```\n\nSee `docs/runbooks/network-policy-escape-hatch.md` for full procedure.\n\n## Kickstarting Stalled HelmReleases\n\nHelmReleases can get stuck in a `Stalled` state with `RetriesExceeded` even after the underlying issue is resolved. This happens because:\n\n1. The HR hit its retry limit (default: 4 attempts)\n2. The failure counter persists even if pods are now healthy\n3. Flux won''t auto-retry once `Stalled` condition is set\n\n**Symptoms:**\n```\nSTATUS: Stalled\nMESSAGE: Failed to install after 4 attempt(s)\nREASON: RetriesExceeded\n```\n\n**Diagnosis:** Check if the underlying resources are actually healthy:\n```bash\n# HR shows Failed, but check if pods are running\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml kubectl get pods -n <namespace> -l app.kubernetes.io/name=<app>\n\n# If pods are Running but HR is Stalled, the HR just needs a reset\n```\n\n**Fix:** Suspend and resume to reset the failure counter:\n```bash\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml flux suspend helmrelease <name> -n flux-system\nKUBECONFIG=~/.kube/<cluster>.yaml flux resume helmrelease <name> -n flux-system\n```\n\n**Common causes of initial failure (that may have self-healed):**\n- Missing Secret/ConfigMap (ExternalSecret eventually created it)\n- Missing CRD (operator finished installing)\n- Transient network issues during image pull\n- Resource quota temporarily exceeded\n\n**Prevention:** Ensure proper `dependsOn` ordering so prerequisites are ready before HelmRelease installs.\n\n## Promotion Pipeline Debugging\n\n**Symptom: \"Live cluster not updating after merge\"**\n\nThe OCI artifact promotion pipeline has multiple stages where failures can stall deployment.\nWalk through each stage in order to find where the pipeline is stuck.\n\n### Diagnostic Steps\n\n```\n1. PR merged to main\n   └─ Check: Did build-platform-artifact.yaml trigger?\n      └─ GitHub Actions → \"Build Platform Artifact\" workflow\n      └─ If missing: Was kubernetes/ modified? (paths filter)\n\n2. OCI artifact built\n   └─ Check: Is the artifact in GHCR with integration-* tag?\n      └─ flux list artifact oci://ghcr.io/<repo>/platform | grep integration\n\n3. Integration cluster picks up artifact\n   └─ Check: Does OCIRepository see the new version?\n      └─ KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/integration.yaml kubectl get ocirepository -n flux-system\n      └─ Look at .status.artifact.revision — does it match the new RC tag?\n      └─ If stale: Check semver constraint (must be \">= 0.0.0-0\" to accept RCs)\n\n4. Integration reconciliation succeeds\n   └─ Check: Platform Kustomization healthy?\n      └─ KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/integration.yaml flux get kustomizations -n flux-system\n      └─ If failed: Read Kustomization events for the error\n\n5. Flux Alert fires repository_dispatch\n   └─ Check: Did the Alert fire?\n      └─ KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/integration.yaml kubectl describe alert validation-success -n flux-system\n      └─ Check Provider (GitHub) status:\n         KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/integration.yaml kubectl get providers -n flux-system\n\n6. tag-validated-artifact.yaml runs\n   └─ Check: Did the workflow trigger?\n      └─ GitHub Actions → \"Tag Validated Artifact\" workflow\n      └─ If not triggered: repository_dispatch may not have fired\n         (check Provider secret has repo scope)\n      └─ If triggered but failed: Check workflow logs for tagging errors\n\n7. Live cluster picks up validated artifact\n   └─ Check: Does OCIRepository see the stable semver?\n      └─ KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/live.yaml kubectl get ocirepository -n flux-system\n      └─ Semver constraint must be \">= 0.0.0\" (stable only, no RCs)\n```\n\n### Common Failure Modes\n\n| Stage | Symptom | Common Cause |\n|-------|---------|--------------|\n| Build | Workflow did not trigger | `kubernetes/` not in changed paths |\n| Build | Artifact push failed | GHCR auth issue (`GITHUB_TOKEN` permissions) |\n| Integration | OCIRepository not updating | Semver constraint mismatch (not accepting RCs) |\n| Validation | Kustomization failed | Actual config error in the merged PR |\n| Promotion | `repository_dispatch` not received | Provider secret missing `repo` scope |\n| Promotion | Workflow skipped (idempotency guard) | Artifact already tagged as validated |\n| Live | OCIRepository not updating | Stable semver tag not created by tag workflow |\n\n### Manual Promotion (Emergency)\n\nIf the pipeline is stuck and live needs the update:\n\n```bash\n# Authenticate to GHCR\necho $GITHUB_TOKEN | docker login ghcr.io -u $GITHUB_USER --password-stdin\n\n# Find the integration artifact\nflux list artifact oci://ghcr.io/<repo>/platform | grep integration\n\n# Manually tag as validated + stable semver\nflux tag artifact oci://ghcr.io/<repo>/platform:<rc-tag> --tag <stable-semver>\n```\n\nSee `.github/CLAUDE.md` for full pipeline architecture and rollback procedures.\n\n## Common Confusions\n\nBAD: Jump to logs without checking events first\nGOOD: Events provide context, then investigate logs\n\nBAD: Look only at current pod state\nGOOD: Check `--previous` logs if pod restarted\n\nBAD: Assume first error is root cause\nGOOD: Apply 5 Whys to find true root cause\n\nBAD: Investigate without confirming cluster\nGOOD: ALWAYS confirm cluster before any kubectl command\n\n## Keywords\n\nkubernetes, debugging, crashloopbackoff, oomkilled, pending, root cause analysis, 5 whys, incident investigation, pod logs, events, troubleshooting, network policy, hubble, stalled helmrelease, promotion pipeline, live not updating\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:32:50.056Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing advanced Kubernetes incident debugging capabilities with 5 Whys Analysis and Multi-Source Correlation","zh":"非常适合需要高级Kubernetes故障调试能力的DevOps代理，包括5 Whys分析和多源关联","ja":"DevOpsエージェントがKubernetesのインシデントのデバッグを行う際に高度な分析機能を必要とする場合に最適です。5 Whys分析やマルチソース関連付けが可能です","ko":"고급 Kubernetes 인시던트 디버깅 기능과 5 Whys 분석 및 멀티소스 상관분석이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de depuración de incidentes de Kubernetes con Análisis de 5 Whys y Correlación Multi-Fuente","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps nécessitant des capacités de débogage avancées d''incident Kubernetes avec Analyse 5 Whys et Corrélation Multi-Source","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die erweiterte Kubernetes-Incident-Debugging-Funktionen mit 5-Whys-Analyse und Multi-Quellen-Korrelation benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para agentes DevOps que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de depuração de incidentes do Kubernetes com Análise de 5 Whys e Correlação Multi-Fonte","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым необходимы расширенные возможности отладки инцидентов Kubernetes с помощью анализа 5 Whys и многозначной корреляции","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتصحيح أخطاء حوادث Kubernetes مع تحليل 5 Whys وتعاون متعدد المصادر"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform read-only investigations of Kubernetes clusters using KUBECONFIG patterns, internal service URLs, and metrics analysis, enabling root cause identification with tools like 5 Whys Analysis","zh":"赋予代理使用KUBECONFIG模式、内部服务URL和指标分析进行Kubernetes集群的只读调查的能力，能够使用5 Whys分析等工具进行根因识别","ja":"エージェントがKUBECONFIGパターン、内部サービスURL、およびメトリクス分析を使用してKubernetesクラスターの読み取り専用の調査を行うことを可能にします。5 Whys分析などのツールを使用して根本原因を特定できます","ko":"에이전트가 KUBECONFIG 패턴, 내부 서비스 URL 및 메트릭 분석을 사용하여 Kubernetes 클러스터의 읽기 전용 조사를 수행할 수 있도록 합니다. 5 Whys 분석과 같은 도구를 사용하여 근본 원인을 식별할 수 있습니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones de solo lectura de clusters de Kubernetes utilizando patrones de KUBECONFIG, URLs de servicios internos y análisis de métricas, lo que permite la identificación de causas raíz con herramientas como Análisis de 5 Whys","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des investigations en lecture seule de clusters Kubernetes en utilisant des modèles de KUBECONFIG, des URL de services internes et une analyse de métriques, permettant l''identification de la cause profonde avec des outils comme l''Analyse 5 Whys","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, nur-Lese-Untersuchungen von Kubernetes-Clustern durchzuführen, indem KUBECONFIG-Muster, interne Dienst-URLs und Metrikanalysen verwendet werden, sodass die Identifizierung der Ursache mit Tools wie 5-Whys-Analyse ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar investigações somente leitura de clusters Kubernetes usando padrões KUBECONFIG, URLs de serviços internos e análise de métricas, permitindo a identificação da causa raiz com ferramentas como a Análise de 5 Whys","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить только чтение расследований кластеров Kubernetes с помощью шаблонов KUBECONFIG, внутренних URL-адресов служб и анализа метрик, что позволяет определять коренную причину с помощью инструментов, таких как анализ 5 Whys","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء تحقيقات قراءة فقط للclusters Kubernetes باستخدام أنماط KUBECONFIG وURLs الخدمات الداخلية وتحليل المقاييس، مما يمكّن من تحديد السبب الجذري بأدوات مثل تحليل 5 Whys"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging Kubernetes incidents with multi-source correlation of logs, events, and metrics","Performing 5 Whys Analysis to identify root causes of cluster issues","Conducting read-only investigations of live clusters to minimize disruption"],"zh":["使用多源日志、事件和指标关联进行Kubernetes故障调试","执行5 Whys分析以识别集群问题的根因","对实时集群进行只读调查以最小化中断"],"ja":["ログ、イベント、メトリクスのマルチソース関連付けを使用したKubernetesのインシデントのデバッグ","5 Whys分析を実行してクラスターの問題の根本原因を特定する","実行中のクラスターの読み取り専用の調査を実行して中断を最小限に抑える"],"ko":["멀티소스 로그, 이벤트 및 메트릭 상관분석을 사용하여 Kubernetes 인시던트 디버깅","5 Whys 분석을 수행하여 클러스터 문제의 근본 원인을 식별","실시간 클러스터에 대한 읽기 전용 조사 수행하여 중단 최소화"],"es":["Depuración de incidentes de Kubernetes con correlación multi-fuente de registros, eventos y métricas","Realizar Análisis de 5 Whys para identificar las causas raíz de los problemas del clúster","Realizar investigaciones de solo lectura de clústeres en vivo para minimizar la interrupción"],"fr":["Débogage d''incidents Kubernetes avec corrélation multi-source de journaux, d''événements et de métriques","Réalisant l''Analyse 5 Whys pour identifier les causes profondes des problèmes de cluster","Effectuant des investigations en lecture seule de clusters en direct pour minimiser les perturbations"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Kubernetes-Incidenten mit Multi-Quellen-Korrelation von Protokollen, Ereignissen und Metriken","Durchführung der 5-Whys-Analyse, um die Ursachen von Clusterproblemen zu identifizieren","Durchführung von nur-Lese-Untersuchungen von Live-Clustern, um Störungen zu minimieren"],"pt":["Depuração de incidentes do Kubernetes com correlação multi-fonte de logs, eventos e métricas","Realização da Análise de 5 Whys para identificar as causas raiz dos problemas do cluster","Realização de investigações somente leitura de clusters ao vivo para minimizar a interrupção"],"ru":["Отладка инцидентов Kubernetes с многозначной корреляцией журналов, событий и метрик","Проведение анализа 5 Whys для определения коренных причин проблем кластера","Проведение только чтение расследований живых кластеров для минимизации сбоев"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء حوادث Kubernetes مع تعاون متعدد المصادر لالسجلات والأحداث والمقاييس","إجراء تحليل 5 Whys لتحديد الأسباب الجذري لحوادث Cluster","إجراء تحقيقات قراءة فقط للclusters الحية لتقليل الإضطراب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to KUBECONFIG and internal service URLs","Limited to debugging and investigation, not suitable for direct resource modification on live clusters"],"zh":["需要访问KUBECONFIG和内部服务URL","仅限于调试和调查，不适合直接在实时集群上修改资源"],"ja":["KUBECONFIGと内部サービスURLへのアクセスが必要","デバッグと調査のみに限定され、実行中のクラスターでの直接リソースの変更には不適"],"ko":["KUBECONFIG 및 내부 서비스 URL에 대한 액세스가 필요","디버깅 및 조사만 가능하며 실시간 클러스터에서의 직접 리소스 수정에는 부적합"],"es":["Requiere acceso a KUBECONFIG y URLs de servicios internos","Limitado a la depuración y la investigación, no apto para la modificación directa de recursos en clústeres en vivo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à KUBECONFIG et aux URL de services internes","Limité au débogage et à l''investigation, non adapté à la modification directe de ressources sur des clusters en direct"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf KUBECONFIG und interne Dienst-URLs","Begrenzt auf Fehlersuche und Untersuchung, nicht geeignet für direkte Ressourcenmodifikation auf Live-Clustern"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao KUBECONFIG e às URLs de serviços internos","Limitado à depuração e investigação, não adequado para modificação direta de recursos em clusters ao vivo"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к KUBECONFIG и внутренним URL-адресам служб","Ограничен отладкой и расследованием, не подходит для прямого изменения ресурсов в живых кластерах"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى KUBECONFIG وURLs الخدمات الداخلية","محدود بتصحيح الأخطاء والتحقيق، لا يصلح لتغيير مباشر للموارد في clusters الحية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3ecc82e2345263462a1fff3054846a29c1678cd4cf79113c169f6da11c8a322c","qualityScore":45}');
