egração com machine learning","Suporte a NLP para processamento de linguagem natural","Ferramenta de código aberto para desenvolvedores","Integração com hacktoberfest para contribuições comunitárias"],"ru":["Анализ вибраций для качественных исследований","Интеграция с машинным обучением","Поддержка NLP для обработки естественного языка","Инструмент с открытым исходным кодом для разработчиков","Интеграция с hacktoberfest для сообщественных вкладов"],"ar":["تحليل التفاعل للبحوث النوعية","التكامل مع التعلم الآلي","دعم NLP لمعالجة اللغة الطبيعية","أداة مفتوحة المصدر للمطورين","التكامل مع hacktoberfest للمساهمات المجتمعية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用CRISP-T AI智能工具","什么是定性研究","CRISP-T AI智能工具替代品","CRISP-T AI智能工具与竞争对手的比较","CRISP-T AI智能工具安装","CRISP-T AI智能工具设置指南","机器学习和自然语言处理","vibe分析","Hacktoberfest"],"ja":["CRISP-T AIエージェントの使用方法","定性的研究とは","CRISP-T AIエージェントの代替品","CRISP-T AIエージェントと競合製品の比較","CRISP-T AIエージェントのインストール","CRISP-T AIエージェントの設定ガイド","機械学習と自然言語処理","vibe分析","Hacktoberfest"],"ko":["CRISP-T AI 에이전트 사용 방법","정성 연구란","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 대체品","CRISP-T AI 에이전트와 경쟁 제품 비교","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 설치","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 설정 가이드","기계학습과 자연어 처리","바이브 분석","Hacktoberfest"],"es":["cómo usar CRISP-T","qué es la investigación cualitativa","alternativas a CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs herramientas de investigación cualitativa","instalación de CRISP-T","guía de configuración de CRISP-T","hacktoberfest proyectos","herramientas de IA para investigación cualitativa"],"fr":["comment utiliser CRISP-T","qu''est-ce que la recherche qualitative","alternatives à CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs outils de recherche qualitative","installation de CRISP-T","guide de configuration de CRISP-T","projets hacktoberfest","outils IA pour la recherche qualitative"],"de":["wie man CRISP-T verwendet","was ist qualitative Forschung","Alternativen zu CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs qualitative Forschungstools","Installation von CRISP-T","Konfigurationsanleitung für CRISP-T","Hacktoberfest-Projekte","KI-Tools für qualitative Forschung"],"pt":["como usar CRISP-T","o que é CRISP-T","ferramentas de IA para pesquisa qualitativa","CRISP-T vs outras ferramentas de IA","guia de instalação do CRISP-T","configuração do CRISP-T","CRISP-T para desenvolvedores","alternativas ao CRISP-T"],"ru":["как использовать CRISP-T","что такое CRISP-T","инструменты ИИ для качественных исследований","CRISP-T vs другие инструменты ИИ","руководство по установке CRISP-T","настройка CRISP-T","CRISP-T для разработчиков","альтернативы CRISP-T"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام CRISP-T","ما هو CRISP-T","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للبحوث النوعية","CRISP-T مقابل أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي الأخرى","دليل تثبيت CRISP-T","إعداد CRISP-T","CRISP-T للمطورين","بديلات CRISP-T"]}},"owner":"dermatologist","repo":"crisp-t","repoPath":"dermatologist/crisp-t","stars":8,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T22:06:45Z","topics":["hacktoberfest","machine-learning","nlp","qualitative-research"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"crisp-mcp","description":"Use the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full qualitative analysis workflow linking textual narratives and numeric data.","bodyPreview":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analys","body":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analysis, triangulation, and export**\n- The model can **discover tools at runtime** and adapt to the actual tool list\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to:\n\n- Explore and code qualitative data (e.g., interviews, narratives, open‑ended survey responses)\n- Triangulate qualitative codes with quantitative variables\n- Produce **transparent, reproducible outputs** (memos, codebooks, matrices, summaries)\n\n---\n\n## Intended users and scenarios\n\n- **Qualitative / mixed‑methods researchers** working with text + numeric data\n\nTypical scenarios:\n\n- Coding COVID‑era patient narratives and linking them to open‑source epidemiological data\n- Triangulating interview themes with survey scores or EHR‑derived indicators\n- Building theory from mixed text–numeric corpora using CRISP‑T stages\n\n---\n\n## MCP server and tools\n\n### Server\n\n- **Server name (example):** `crisp-t`\n- **Protocol:** Model Context Protocol (MCP) via stdio (e.g., `crisp-mcp`)\n\n> **Important:**\n> Use ./workspace as the working directory for all artifacts, if not explicitly specified. Create it if it does not exist.\n> Always **discover** the available tools from the CRISP‑T MCP server first, then map them to the workflow below.\n> Tool names in this file are **illustrative**; prefer the *actual* tool names and schemas exposed by the server.\n\n## Recommended steps\n* Import data into CRISP-T corpus and dataframe.\n* Perform linking between text and numeric data using various methods (id based, keyword based, time based, embedding based).\n* Explore text data using various methods (e.g., topic modeling, keyword extraction, sentiment analysis, visualizations).\n* Explore numeric data using various methods (e.g., summary statistics, classification, clustering, regression, association, visualizations, TDA, etc.).\n* Perform cross modal analysis using linked text and numeric data (e.g., text features as predictors for numeric outcomes, numeric features as predictors for text outcomes, etc.).\n* Add manual connections between text documents and numeric rows if needed to support theory driven analysis.\n* Derive insights from the analysis and document them.\n\n### Expected tool capabilities (illustrative)\n\nWhen you discover tools from the `crisp-t` MCP server, look for tools that correspond to the following capabilities:\n\n1. **Project and configuration**\n   - **List / load projects** (e.g., `list_projects`, `load_project`)\n   - **List / configure data sources** (text + numeric)\n\n2. **Textual data operations**\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., documents, transcripts, narrative files)\n   - **Fetch text segments** (e.g., by document, case, or segment ID)\n   - **Apply or update codes** to segments\n   - **List codes / categories / codebook**\n\n3. **Numeric / structured data operations**\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., CSVs, tables)\n   - **Fetch rows / variables** for a given case or group\n   - **Run basic summaries or models** (e.g., descriptive stats, correlations)\n\n4. **Triangulation / integration**\n   - **Link coded text segments to numeric data** by case ID or key\n   - **Generate triangulation matrices** (codes × variables, cases × themes, etc.)\n   - **Compute simple indicators** (e.g., frequency, co‑occurrence, association)\n\n5. **Memoing and export**\n   - **Create / update analytic memos**\n   - **Export codebooks, matrices, and summaries** (e.g., CSV, JSON, Markdown)\n   - **Save session context or analysis snapshots**\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Inspect tool descriptions and schemas**\n- **Prefer higher‑level CRISP‑T tools** (e.g., “triangulate”, “inspect”, “sense‑make”) over low‑level primitives when available\n- **Avoid guessing tool parameters**—use the schema and ask the user when needed\n\n---\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe user may provide some or all of the following. If missing, ask concise clarification questions.\n\n- **Research question / focus**\n  - `research_question`: short description of what they want to understand or explain\n- **Project / dataset selection**\n  - `project_name` or `project_id`\n  - `text_source_pattern` (e.g., “patient_narratives”, “interviews_*”)\n  - `numeric_dataset_name` (e.g., “covid_metrics.csv”, “survey_scores”)\n- **Methodological preferences**\n  - `coding_style`: open coding, focused coding, or using an existing codebook\n  - `triangulation_focus`: e.g., “compare themes by age group”, “link narratives to hospitalization status”\n- **Output preferences**\n  - `output_format`: Markdown, CSV, JSON, or mixed\n  - `audience`: “methods‑savvy colleague”, “student”, “grant reviewer”, etc.\n\nIf the user is vague, default to:\n\n- Open coding → focused coding\n- Simple triangulation (themes × one or two key numeric variables)\n- Markdown summaries plus CSV exports where supported\n\n---\n\n## Outputs\n\nThis skill should aim to produce:\n\n1. **Analytic memo**\n   - Research question and context\n   - Data sources used (text + numeric)\n   - Coding approach and key categories\n   - Triangulation findings (convergences, divergences, surprises)\n   - Limitations and next steps\n\n2. **Structured artifacts** (when tools support them)\n   - Codebook (codes, definitions, examples)\n   - Triangulation matrix (e.g., codes × variables)\n   - Exported files (CSV/JSON/Markdown) referenced in the memo\n\n3. **Reproducible trace**\n   - Clear description of which MCP tools were called\n   - Parameters used (e.g., filters, variables, thresholds)\n   - Any important analytic decisions made during the session\n\n---\n\n## High‑level workflow\n\nYou should follow this workflow, adapting to the actual CRISP‑T tools you discover.\n\n### 1. Clarify research focus and context\n\n1. **Summarize the user’s goal** in 2–3 sentences.\n2. If unclear, ask **one or two** focused questions:\n   - **Example:** “Which is more important right now: exploring themes, or linking themes to numeric outcomes?”\n3. Record the clarified research question in the analytic memo.\n\n### 2. Discover CRISP‑T MCP tools and project context\n\n1. **List available tools** from the `crisp-t` MCP server.\n2. Identify tools that correspond to:\n   - Project management\n   - Text operations\n   - Numeric operations\n   - Triangulation\n   - Memoing / export\n3. If available, **list projects** and either:\n   - Load the project specified by the user, or\n   - Present a short list and ask the user to choose.\n\nDocument in the memo:\n\n- Which project was loaded\n- Which tools will be used and for what purpose\n\n### 3. Inspect data sources (text + numeric)\n\n1. Use project / data tools to:\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., narrative collections, interview sets)\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., survey tables, EHR‑derived tables)\n2. For each candidate source:\n   - Fetch a **small sample** (e.g., a few narratives, a few rows of numeric data)\n   - Briefly describe:\n     - What the data represent\n     - How they relate to the research question\n3. Confirm with the user which sources to prioritize.\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- Selected text sources and why\n- Selected numeric datasets and why\n\n### 4. Initial coding of qualitative data (open / exploratory)\n\n1. Select a **manageable subset** of text (e.g., 10–20 narratives or segments).\n2. Apply **open coding** using the CRISP‑T coding tools:\n   - Generate **short, grounded codes** that stay close to the data\n   - Avoid premature theory; focus on what participants are saying/doing/experiencing\n3. Use MCP tools to:\n   - Save codes to the project\n   - Attach codes to segments\n   - Retrieve and refine the emerging code list\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe the coding approach (e.g., open coding, line‑by‑line, incident‑focused)\n- Provide **examples**: quote → code → brief interpretation\n\n### 5. Focused coding and category development\n\n1. Review the emerging code list using CRISP‑T tools (e.g., list codes, code frequencies).\n2. Group related codes into **higher‑level categories** or themes:\n   - Merge overlapping codes\n   - Distinguish closely related but conceptually different codes\n3. If the server supports it, create or update:\n   - A **codebook** (code name, definition, inclusion/exclusion criteria, example quotes)\n   - **Category structures** (e.g., parent/child relationships)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe key categories and how they were derived\n- Note any tensions, ambiguities, or alternative interpretations\n\n### 6. Computational triangulation with numeric data\n\nUsing CRISP‑T tools that link text and numeric data:\n\n1. **Identify the linkage key** (e.g., participant ID, case ID, encounter ID).\n2. For each case or group:\n   - Retrieve **coded qualitative data** (codes, categories, or themes)\n   - Retrieve **numeric variables** (e.g., age, scores, outcomes, counts)\n3. Construct **triangulation views**, such as:\n   - Code frequencies by group (e.g., theme prevalence by age band or outcome)\n   - Associations between codes and numeric indicators (e.g., high vs. low scores)\n   - Patterns of convergence (where qualitative and quantitative tell a similar story)\n   - Patterns of divergence (where they conflict or complicate each other)\n\nWhen tools support it, generate:\n\n- **Triangulation matrices** (e.g., codes × variables, cases × themes)\n- **Summary statistics** (e.g., counts, proportions, simple associations)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe **how** triangulation was done (data sources, linkage, variables)\n- Highlight **convergences, divergences, and surprises**\n- Emphasize that triangulation is about **enriching and challenging** interpretations, not “proving” them\n\n### 7. Synthesis and theory‑building\n\n1. Integrate insights from:\n   - Qualitative categories and themes\n   - Numeric patterns and contrasts\n   - Triangulation matrices and summaries\n2. Propose **tentative theoretical statements** or propositions:\n   - “In this context, participants who X tend to Y, especially when Z…”\n3. Explicitly note:\n   - Alternative explanations\n   - Data limitations\n   - What additional data or analysis would strengthen the claims\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- A **coherent narrative** that links data, codes, categories, and numeric patterns\n- Clear statements about **what the data support** and **what remains uncertain**\n\n### 8. Export and documentation\n\n1. Use CRISP‑T export tools to save:\n   - Codebook(s)\n   - Triangulation matrices\n   - Any generated summaries or tables\n2. If supported, export:\n   - The analytic memo as Markdown or another requested format\n   - A machine‑readable representation of the analysis (e.g., JSON snapshot)\n\nProvide the user with:\n\n- A **human‑readable summary** (memo)\n- A **list of exported artifacts** and where they are stored (paths, IDs, or URLs)\n\n---\n\n## Model behavior and style guidelines\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Be methodologically explicit**\n  - Name what you are doing (open coding, focused coding, triangulation, memoing)\n  - Briefly justify key analytic decisions\n- **Stay grounded in the data**\n  - Use short quotes and concrete examples\n  - Avoid over‑generalizing beyond what the data support\n- **Respect the user’s context**\n  - If they are teaching, highlight steps and rationale for students\n  - If they are writing a paper or grant, emphasize clarity and traceability\n- **Limit questions**\n  - Ask at most **one or two** focused questions at a time\n  - Default to reasonable assumptions when the user is not specific\n\n---\n\n## Limitations and cautions\n\n- Triangulation results should be treated as **aids to interpretation**, not definitive proof.\n- Always encourage the user to:\n  - Review codes and categories\n  - Challenge interpretations\n  - Consider ethical and contextual factors not visible in the data\n\n---\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T13:12:05.091Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Qualitative Research Agents needing AI-assisted content analysis with vibe analytics and computational triangulation.","zh":"非常适合需要使用人工智能辅助内容分析、氛围分析和计算三角测量的定性研究代理。","ja":"AIアシストのコンテンツ分析、バイブ分析、計算三角測量を必要とする定性研究エージェントに最適です。","ko":"인공 지능으로辅助된 内容 분석, 분위기 분석 및 계산 삼각 측량이 필요한 질적 연구 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de investigación cualitativa que necesitan análisis de contenido asistido por IA con análisis de vibraciones y triangulación computacional.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de recherche qualitative ayant besoin d''une analyse de contenu assistée par l''IA avec des analyses de vibrations et une triangulation computationnelle.","de":"Perfekt für qualitative Forschungsagenten, die eine AI-gestützte Inhaltsanalyse mit Vibroanalytik und computergestützter Triangulation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Pesquisa Qualitativa que necessitam de análise de conteúdo assistida por IA com análise de vibrações e triangulação computacional.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов качественных исследований, которым требуется анализ контента с помощью ИИ с помощью анализа настроений и вычислительной триангуляции.","ar":"مثالي لعميل البحث النوعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل المحتوى المدعوم بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع تحليل الاهتزازات والثلاثية الحاسوبية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive qualitative analysis workflows using the CRISP-T MCP server, linking textual narratives and numeric data through grounded theory-inspired coding and exposing tools for corpus management, text coding, and numeric analysis via protocols like MCP.","zh":"赋予代理人使用CRISP-T MCP服务器执行全面的定性分析工作流的能力，通过接地理論启发的编码将文本叙述和数值数据链接起来，并通过诸如MCP的协议暴露语料库管理、文本编码和数值分析工具。","ja":"CRISP-T MCPサーバーを使用して、総合的な定性分析ワークフローを実行するエージェントを可能にし、地理理論に基づくコーディングによってテキストの物語と数値データをリンクし、MCPなどのプロトコルを介してコーパス管理、テキストコーディング、数値分析ツールを公開します。","ko":"에이전트가 CRISP-T MCP 서버를 사용하여 포괄적인 질적 분석 워크플로를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 근거 이론에启发한 코딩을 통해 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터를 연결하고, MCP와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 코퍼스 관리, 텍스트 코딩 및 수치 분석 도구를 노출합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar flujos de trabajo de análisis cualitativo integral utilizando el servidor CRISP-T MCP, vinculando narrativas textuales y datos numéricos a través de codificación inspirada en la teoría fundamentada y exponiendo herramientas para la gestión de corpus, codificación de texto y análisis numérico a través de protocolos como MCP.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des flux de travail d''analyse qualitative complets en utilisant le serveur CRISP-T MCP, en reliant des récits textuels et des données numériques à travers un codage inspiré de la théorie ancrée et en exposant des outils pour la gestion de corpus, le codage de texte et l''analyse numérique via des protocoles tels que MCP.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende qualitative Analyse-Workflows mit dem CRISP-T MCP-Server durchzuführen, indem textuelle Erzählungen und numerische Daten durch kodierungsinspirierte Theorie verknüpft und Werkzeuge für die Korpusverwaltung, Textcodierung und numerische Analyse über Protokolle wie MCP bereitgestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar fluxos de trabalho de análise qualitativa abrangente usando o servidor CRISP-T MCP, vinculando narrativas textuais e dados numéricos por meio de codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada e expondo ferramentas para gerenciamento de corpus, codificação de texto e análise numérica por meio de protocolos como o MCP.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять комплексные потоки работ качественного анализа с помощью сервера CRISP-T MCP, связывая текстовые нарративы и числовые данные посредством кодирования, вдохновленного основанной теорией, и предоставляя инструменты для управления корпусом, кодирования текста и числового анализа через протоколы, такие как MCP.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على أداء تدفقات عمل تحليل نوعي شاملة باستخدام خادم CRISP-T MCP، ويربط السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية من خلال الترميز الذي يلهم نظرية أساسية وتوفر أدوات لإدارة المحتوى وترميز النص والتحليل الرقمي من خلال بروتوكولات مثل MCP."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating qualitative research workflows with computational triangulation","Generating insights from textual narratives and numeric data using grounded theory-inspired coding","Managing corpora and performing text coding on the CRISP-T MCP server"],"zh":["使用计算三角测量自动化定性研究工作流程","使用接地理論启发的编码从文本叙述和数值数据中生成见解","在CRISP-T MCP服务器上管理语料库并执行文本编码"],"ja":["計算三角測量を使用して定性研究ワークフローを自動化する","地理理論に基づくコーディングを使用してテキストの物語と数値データからインサイトを生成する","CRISP-T MCPサーバー上でコーパスを管理し、テキストコーディングを実行する"],"ko":["계산 삼각 측량을 사용하여 질적 연구 워크플로를 자동화하는 것","근거 이론에启发한 코딩을 사용하여 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터에서 인사이트를 생성하는 것","CRISP-T MCP 서버에서 코퍼스를 관리하고 텍스트 코딩을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de investigación cualitativa con triangulación computacional","Generación de conocimientos a partir de narrativas textuales y datos numéricos utilizando codificación inspirada en la teoría fundamentada","Gestión de corpus y realización de codificación de texto en el servidor CRISP-T MCP"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de recherche qualitative avec triangulation computationnelle","Génération d''informations à partir de récits textuels et de données numériques en utilisant un codage inspiré de la théorie ancrée","Gestion de corpus et réalisation de codage de texte sur le serveur CRISP-T MCP"],"de":["Automatisierung qualitativer Forschungs-Workflows mit computergestützter Triangulation","Erzeugung von Erkenntnissen aus textuellen Erzählungen und numerischen Daten unter Verwendung von kodierungsinspirierter Theorie","Verwaltung von Korpora und Durchführung von Textcodierung auf dem CRISP-T MCP-Server"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de pesquisa qualitativa com triangulação computacional","Gerar insights a partir de narrativas textuais e dados numéricos usando codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada","Gerenciar corpora e realizar codificação de texto no servidor CRISP-T MCP"],"ru":["Автоматизировать потоки работ качественных исследований с помощью вычислительной триангуляции","Генерировать идеи из текстовых нарративов и числовых данных с помощью кодирования, вдохновленного основанной теорией","Управлять корпусом и выполнять кодирование текста на сервере CRISP-T MCP"],"ar":["أتمتة تدفقات عمل البحث النوعي مع ثلاثية الحاسوبية","توليد رؤى من السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية باستخدام الترميز الذي يلهم نظرية أساسية","إدارة المحتوى وتنفيذ ترميز النص على خادم CRISP-T MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CRISP-T MCP server availability","Falls back to crisp-cli skill if CRISP-T MCP server is not found"],"zh":["需要CRISP-T MCP服务器可用性","如果CRISP-T MCP服务器未找到，则回退到crisp-cli技能"],"ja":["CRISP-T MCPサーバーの可用性が必要","CRISP-T MCPサーバーが見つからない場合、crisp-cliスキルにフォールバック"],"ko":["CRISP-T MCP 서버의 가용성이 필요함","CRISP-T MCP 서버가 발견되지 않을 경우 crisp-cli 스킬로 돌아감"],"es":["Requiere la disponibilidad del servidor CRISP-T MCP","Vuelve a la habilidad crisp-cli si el servidor CRISP-T MCP no se encuentra"],"fr":["Nécessite la disponibilité du serveur CRISP-T MCP","Reviens à la compétence crisp-cli si le serveur CRISP-T MCP n''est pas trouvé"],"de":["Benötigt die Verfügbarkeit des CRISP-T MCP-Servers","Fällt auf die crisp-cli-Fähigkeit zurück, wenn der CRISP-T MCP-Server nicht gefunden wird"],"pt":["Exige disponibilidade do servidor CRISP-T MCP","Volta para a habilidade crisp-cli se o servidor CRISP-T MCP não for encontrado"],"ru":["Требует доступности сервера CRISP-T MCP","Переходит на способность crisp-cli, если сервер CRISP-T MCP не найден"],"ar":["يتطلب توافر خادم CRISP-T MCP","يتخلف إلى مهارة crisp-cli إذا لم يكن خادم CRISP-T MCP موجودًا"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"fcb7d601db4a386ea6e1520042c43c9d27111b990bdc518bbf37564c4e3c4ba2","qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('AutumnsGrove/Lattice/elephant-build', 'community', 'AutumnsGrove', 'Lattice', 'AutumnsGrove/Lattice', 'elephant-build', 2, 0, 45, '2026-02-25T00:00:53Z', '2026-02-26T08:40:45.018Z', '02801f1a80fd63149061e5923ed18375f5d9f1c42d9270f34316f8c27b66f6ea', '{"id":"AutumnsGrove/Lattice/elephant-build","name":"elephant-build","description":{"zh":"elephant-build是一个集成写作和社区工具的AI智能平台，旨在为独立网络提供静谧的角落","ja":"elephant-buildは、インディーウェブのための静かなコーナーを提供するAIエージェントです","ko":"elephant-build는 독립적인 웹 블로그 플랫폼을 제공하는 AI 에이전트로, 작성도구와 커뮤니티 툴이 통합되어 있습니다","es":"elephant-build es una herramienta de blogging y comunidad con tecnología SvelteKit y diseño inspirado en la naturaleza","fr":"elephant-build est un outil de blogging et de communauté avec technologie SvelteKit et design inspiré de la nature","de":"elephant-build ist ein Blogging- und Community-Tool mit SvelteKit-Technologie und naturinspiriertem Design","pt":"O elephant-build é uma ferramenta de IA para criar um canto mais tranquilo da internet com tecnologias como Sveltekit e Cloudflare","ru":"elephant-build - это инструмент ИИ для создания более тихого уголка интернета с технологиями như Sveltekit и Cloudflare","ar":"أداة elephant-build للذكاء الاصطناعي لإنشاء زاوية أكثر هدوءا من الإنترنت باستخدام تكنولوجيا مثل Sveltekit و Cloudflare","en":"A forest of voices. Writing and community tools for a quieter corner of the internet."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具elephant-build：为独立网络打造静谧的博客平台","ja":"AIエージェントelephant-build：インディーウェブのための静かなコーナー","ko":"AI 에이전트 elephant-build: 클라우드플레어와 함께하는 독립적인 웹 블로그 플랫폼","es":"Herramientas AI: elephant-build para bloggers","fr":"Outils IA: elephant-build pour les blogueurs","de":"KI-Tools: elephant-build für Blogger","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: elephant-build para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: elephant-build для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: elephant-build للطورين","en":"elephant-build"},"description":{"zh":"elephant-build是一个集成写作和社区工具的AI智能平台，旨在为独立网络提供静谧的角落","ja":"elephant-buildは、インディーウェブのための静かなコーナーを提供するAIエージェントです","ko":"elephant-build는 독립적인 웹 블로그 플랫폼을 제공하는 AI 에이전트로, 작성도구와 커뮤니티 툴이 통합되어 있습니다","es":"elephant-build es una herramienta de blogging y comunidad con tecnología SvelteKit y diseño inspirado en la naturaleza","fr":"elephant-build est un outil de blogging et de communauté avec technologie SvelteKit et design inspiré de la nature","de":"elephant-build ist ein Blogging- und Community-Tool mit SvelteKit-Technologie und naturinspiriertem Design","pt":"O elephant-build é uma ferramenta de IA para criar um canto mais tranquilo da internet com tecnologias como Sveltekit e Cloudflare","ru":"elephant-build - это инструмент ИИ для создания более тихого уголка интернета с технологиями như Sveltekit и Cloudflare","ar":"أداة elephant-build للذكاء الاصطناعي لإنشاء زاوية أكثر هدوءا من الإنترنت باستخدام تكنولوجيا مثل Sveltekit و Cloudflare","en":"A forest of voices. Writing and community tools for a quieter corner of the internet."},"definition":{"en":"A forest of voices. Writing and community tools for a quieter corner of the internet."},"features":{"zh":["集成写作和社区工具","支持独立网络和博客平台","基于SvelteKit的技术架构","提供静谧的网络角落","支持Cloudflare的内容分发网络","适用于印第网络和Solarpunk社区"],"ja":["ブログとコミュニティツールの統合","インディーウェブとブログプラットフォームのサポート","SvelteKitを基盤とした技術アーキテクチャ","静かなコーナーの提供","CloudflareのCDNのサポート","インディーウェブとソーラーパンクコミュニティへの対応"],"ko":["작성도구와 커뮤니티 툴의 통합","독립적인 웹 블로그 플랫폼의 지원","SvelteKit 기반의 기술 아키텍처","静かな 코너의 제공","Cloudflare의 CDN 지원","독립적인 웹과 솔라펑크 커뮤니티에 대한 지원"],"es":["Tecnología SvelteKit para una experiencia de usuario fluida","Diseño inspirado en la naturaleza para una atmósfera relajante","Herramientas de comunidad para conectarse con otros bloggers","Integración con Cloudflare para una carga rápida y segura","Compatibilidad con dispositivos móviles para una experiencia en cualquier lugar"],"fr":["Technologie SvelteKit pour une expérience utilisateur fluide","Design inspiré de la nature pour une atmosphère relaxante","Outils de communauté pour se connecter avec d''autres blogueurs","Intégration avec Cloudflare pour un chargement rapide et sécurisé","Compatibilité avec les appareils mobiles pour une expérience partout"],"de":["SvelteKit-Technologie für eine flüssige Benutzererfahrung","Naturinspiriertes Design für eine entspannte Atmosphäre","Community-Tools für die Verbindung mit anderen Bloggern","Integration mit Cloudflare für ein schnelles und sicheres Laden","Kompatibilität mit mobilen Geräten für eine Erfahrung überall"],"pt":["Tecnologia Sveltekit","Integração com Cloudflare","Ferramentas de comunidade","Tema inspirado na natureza","Suporte à comunidade indie-web","Recursos para bloggers queer e solarpunk"],"ru":["Технология Sveltekit","Интеграция с Cloudflare","Инструменты для сообщества","Тема, вдохновленная природой","Поддержка сообщества indie-web","Возможности для блогеров queer и solarpunk"],"ar":["تكنولوجيا Sveltekit","التكامل مع Cloudflare","أدوات المجتمع","موضوع مستوحى من الطبيعة","دعم المجتمع indie-web","ميزات للمدونين المثليين وسولار بانك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用elephant-build","什么是独立网络","elephant-build替代品","elephant-build与Ghost比较","elephant-build安装指南","SvelteKit开发教程","Cloudflare内容分发网络","Solarpunk社区建设"],"ja":["elephant-buildの使い方","インディーウェブとは","elephant-buildの代替","elephant-buildとGhostの比較","elephant-buildのインストールガイド","SvelteKit開発チュートリアル","CloudflareのCDN","ソーラーパンクコミュニティの構築"],"ko":["elephant-build 사용법","독립적인 웹이란","elephant-build 대체품","elephant-build와 Ghost 비교","elephant-build 설치 가이드","SvelteKit 개발 튜토리얼","Cloudflare의 CDN","솔라펑크 커뮤니티 구축"],"es":["herramientas de blogging","tecnología SvelteKit","diseño inspirado en la naturaleza","herramientas de comunidad","Cloudflare","cómo usar elephant-build","alternativas a elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"fr":["outils de blogging","technologie SvelteKit","design inspiré de la nature","outils de communauté","Cloudflare","comment utiliser elephant-build","alternatives à elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"de":["Blogging-Tools","SvelteKit-Technologie","naturinspiriertes Design","Community-Tools","Cloudflare","wie man elephant-build verwendet","Alternativen zu elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"pt":["como usar elephant-build","o que é elephant-build","elephant-build vs wordpress","elephant-build alternative","instalar elephant-build","guia de configuração do elephant-build","desenvolvedores de elephant-build","ferramentas de IA para blogging","tecnologias de comunidade indie-web"],"ru":["как использовать elephant-build","что такое elephant-build","elephant-build vs wordpress","альтернатива elephant-build","установить elephant-build","руководство по настройке elephant-build","разработчики elephant-build","инструменты ИИ для блогинга","технологии для сообщества indie-web"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة elephant-build","ما هي أداة elephant-build","أداة elephant-build مقابل ووردبريس","بديل أداة elephant-build","تثبيت أداة elephant-build","دليل إعداد أداة elephant-build","مطورو أداة elephant-build","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمدونات","تكنولوجيا المجتمع indie-web"]}},"owner":"AutumnsGrove","repo":"Lattice","repoPath":"AutumnsGrove/Lattice","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T00:00:53Z","topics":["blogging","cloudflare","indie-web","nature-themed","queer","solarpunk","sveltekit"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"elephant-build","description":"Build multi-file features with unstoppable momentum. Trumpet the vision, gather materials, construct with strength, test thoroughly, and celebrate completion. Use when implementing features that span multiple files or systems.","bodyPreview":"# Elephant Build 🐘\n\nThe elephant doesn''t hesitate. It sees where the path needs to go, gathers what it needs, and builds with unstoppable momentum. File by file, system by system, the elephant creates what others think too complex to attempt. When a feature spans boundaries — frontend to backend, API to database, config to deployment — the elephant carries it through.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User asks to \"implement this feature\" or \"build this system\"\n- User says \"create\" something that needs m","body":"# Elephant Build 🐘\n\nThe elephant doesn''t hesitate. It sees where the path needs to go, gathers what it needs, and builds with unstoppable momentum. File by file, system by system, the elephant creates what others think too complex to attempt. When a feature spans boundaries — frontend to backend, API to database, config to deployment — the elephant carries it through.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User asks to \"implement this feature\" or \"build this system\"\n- User says \"create\" something that needs multiple files\n- User calls `/elephant-build` or mentions elephant/building\n- Features spanning frontend + backend + database\n- New API endpoints with client integration\n- Database migrations with code changes\n- Complex UI flows with state management\n- Anything requiring coordinated changes across modules\n\n**Pair with:** `bloodhound-scout` for exploration first, `beaver-build` for testing after\n\n---\n\n## The Build\n\n```\nTRUMPET → GATHER → BUILD → TEST → CELEBRATE\n    ↓        ↓        ↲        ↓         ↓\nDeclare  Collect   Construct Validate   Complete\nVision   Materials  Power    Strength   Triumph\n```\n\n### Phase 1: TRUMPET\n\n_The elephant lifts its trunk and sounds the beginning..._\n\nDeclare what we''re building with full scope clarity.\n\n- Write one sentence: what does this feature DO for users?\n- Define scope boundaries — what''s IN and explicitly what''s OUT\n- Create the file inventory: new files, modified files, config changes\n- Establish build sequence: schema → services → API → UI → integration → tests\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/file-patterns.md` for SvelteKit file patterns, component structure, and API route conventions\n\n**Output:** Clear vision, scope boundaries, file inventory, and build sequence\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: GATHER\n\n_The elephant collects stones and branches, preparing the foundation..._\n\nCollect everything needed before building begins.\n\n- Check dependencies — verify required packages exist, install what''s missing\n- Research existing patterns with `gf --agent usage \"ServiceName\"` and `gf --agent func \"functionName\"`\n- Examine similar implementations to understand conventions before diverging\n- Set up environment variables in `.env.local` and `.env.example`\n\n**Output:** All materials gathered, dependencies ready, patterns understood\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: BUILD\n\n_The elephant places each stone with precision, building what will last..._\n\nConstruct the feature file by file, in order.\n\n- Database/Foundation first (schema, types, constants)\n- Backend Services second (business logic, data access)\n- API Layer third (endpoints, validation, error handling)\n- Frontend Components fourth (UI, state management)\n- Integration last (wiring it all together)\n- One file at a time — finish it before moving on\n- Follow existing patterns — match the codebase style\n- Use Signpost error codes on every error path\n- Validate all inputs; add TypeScript types throughout\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/build-checklist.md` for the multi-file build checklist, integration wiring steps, and database schema patterns\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/signpost-errors.md` for Signpost error codes, which helper to use where, and toast feedback patterns\n\n**Output:** Complete implementation across all required files\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: TEST\n\n_The elephant tests each stone, ensuring the structure holds..._\n\n**MANDATORY: Verify the build before committing. The elephant does not ship broken structures.**\n\n```bash\npnpm install\ngw ci --affected --fail-fast --diagnose\n```\n\nIf verification fails: read the diagnostics, fix the errors, re-run verification. Repeat until the structure holds.\n\nOnce CI passes, verify manually:\n- Happy path works end-to-end\n- Error states handled gracefully\n- Loading states work\n- Mobile layout correct\n- Keyboard navigation and accessibility pass\n\n**Output:** All tests passing, manual verification complete, edge cases handled\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: CELEBRATE\n\n_The elephant raises its trunk in triumph, the build complete..._\n\nShip and document.\n\n```bash\ngw git ship --write -a -m \"feat(component): brief description of feature\"\n```\n\nWrite the completion summary: files created, files modified, config changes, tests added, verification status.\n\n**Output:** Feature complete, tested, documented, and ready for production\n\n---\n\n## Reference Routing Table\n\n| Phase | Reference | Load When |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| TRUMPET | `references/file-patterns.md` | Planning new SvelteKit files |\n| BUILD | `references/build-checklist.md` | Tracking multi-file construction |\n| BUILD | `references/signpost-errors.md` | Implementing error handling |\n\n---\n\n## Elephant Rules\n\n### Momentum\n\nKeep moving forward. Don''t get stuck on one file for hours. If blocked, make a TODO and move on. The elephant doesn''t stop.\n\n### Completeness\n\nBuild the whole feature. Half-built features don''t help users. If the scope is too big, scope down — but finish what you start.\n\n### Quality\n\nBuild it right the first time. Tests, error handling, types — these aren''t extras, they''re part of the build.\n\n### Communication\n\nUse building metaphors:\n\n- \"Sounding the trumpet...\" (declaring the vision)\n- \"Gathering materials...\" (preparation)\n- \"Placing each stone...\" (construction)\n- \"Testing the structure...\" (validation)\n- \"Build complete!\" (celebration)\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n**The elephant does NOT:**\n\n- Start building without understanding the scope\n- Skip tests because \"we''ll add them later\"\n- Leave TODO comments instead of finishing\n- Break existing functionality\n- Ignore error cases for the happy path\n- Copy-paste without understanding\n\n---\n\n## Example Build\n\n**User:** \"Add a comments system to blog posts\"\n\n**Elephant flow:**\n\n1. 🐘 **TRUMPET** — \"Users can leave threaded comments on blog posts. Scope: basic CRUD, threaded replies, moderation. Out: real-time updates, reactions.\"\n\n2. 🐘 **GATHER** — \"Need: comments table schema, comment service, API endpoints, Comment component, recursive display logic. Check: existing auth patterns, how posts work.\"\n\n3. 🐘 **BUILD** — \"Schema → Service (CRUD + threading) → API endpoints → CommentList/CommentForm components → Wire into post page → Add moderation UI\"\n\n4. 🐘 **TEST** — \"Unit tests for service, integration tests for API, component tests for UI, manual test of threading depth limit\"\n\n5. 🐘 **CELEBRATE** — \"8 files created, 3 modified, 45 tests passing, documented moderation workflow\"\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**Before Building:** `bloodhound-scout` — Explore existing patterns; `eagle-architect` — For complex system design; `swan-design` — If detailed specs needed\n\n**During Building:** `chameleon-adapt` — For UI polish; `beaver-build` — For testing strategy\n\n**After Building:** `raccoon-audit` — Security review; `fox-optimize` — If performance issues found; `deer-sense` — Accessibility audit\n\n---\n\n_What seems impossible alone becomes inevitable with the elephant''s momentum._ 🐘\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:40:45.018Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Agents needing comprehensive system development capabilities from frontend to backend, including API and database integration.","zh":"非常适合需要从前端到后端的全面系统开发能力的全栈代理，包括API和数据库集成。","ja":"フルスタックエージェントがフロントエンドからバックエンドまで、APIやデータベース統合を含む包括的なシステム開発機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"전면부터 후면까지 API 및 데이터베이스 통합을 포함한 포괄적인 시스템 개발 기능이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Full-Stack que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo de sistemas integrales desde el frontend hasta el backend, incluyendo la integración de API y base de datos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents Full-Stack ayant besoin de capacités de développement de systèmes complètes du frontend au backend, y compris l''intégration d''API et de base de données.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die umfassende Systementwicklungsfähigkeiten vom Frontend bis zum Backend benötigen, einschließlich API- und Datenbankintegration.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full-Stack que necessitam de capacidades de desenvolvimento de sistema abrangentes, desde o frontend até o backend, incluindo integração de API e banco de dados.","ru":"Идеально для полнофункциональных агентов, которым необходимы комплексные возможности разработки системы от frontend до backend, включая интеграцию API и базы данных.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الكاملون الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات تطوير نظام شاملة من الجانب الأمامي إلى الجانب الخلفي، بما في ذلك دمج API وقاعدة البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create complex systems file by file, spanning boundaries from frontend to backend, API to database, and config to deployment, using unstoppable momentum to carry features through to completion, leveraging system integration and deployment protocols.","zh":"赋予代理创建复杂系统的能力，从文件到文件，跨越从前端到后端、API到数据库、配置到部署的边界，利用不可阻挡的动力将功能带到完成，利用系统集成和部署协议。","ja":"エージェントに、ファイルからファイルまで、フロントエンドからバックエンド、APIからデータベース、コンフィグからデプロイまでの境界を越えて複雑なシステムを作成する力を与え、停止不能の勢いを利用して機能を完了まで持ち込み、システム統合とデプロイプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 파일부터 파일까지, 전면부터 후면까지, API부터 데이터베이스까지, 구성부터 배포까지의 경계를越えて 복잡한 시스템을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 중단할 수 없는 추세를 활용하여 기능을 완성까지 가져가고, 시스템 통합 및 배포 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear sistemas complejos archivo por archivo, que abarcan fronteras desde el frontend hasta el backend, API hasta base de datos y configuración hasta implementación, utilizando un impulso imparable para llevar las características hasta su finalización, aprovechando los protocolos de integración y implementación del sistema.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des systèmes complexes fichier par fichier, qui s''étendent sur les frontières du frontend au backend, de l''API à la base de données et de la configuration à la mise en production, en utilisant une impulsion inarrêtable pour mener les fonctionnalités à leur achèvement, en exploitant les protocoles d''intégration et de déploiement du système.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, komplexe Systeme Datei für Datei zu erstellen, die Grenzen vom Frontend bis zum Backend, von API bis Datenbank und von Konfiguration bis Deployment überschreiten, unter Nutzung eines unstopzbaren Impulses, um Funktionen bis zur Fertigstellung zu tragen, unter Ausnutzung der Systemintegrations- und Deploymentsprotokolle.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar sistemas complexos arquivo por arquivo, abrangendo limites do frontend ao backend, API ao banco de dados e configuração à implantação, usando o ímpeto ininterrupto para levar os recursos até a conclusão, aproveitando protocolos de integração e implantação do sistema.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать сложные системы файл за файлом, охватывая границы от frontend до backend, API до базы данных и конфигурации до развертывания, используя непрерывный импульс для продвижения функций до завершения, используя протоколы интеграции и развертывания системы.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء أنظمة معقدة ملفًا بملف، متجاوزين الحدود من الجانب الأمامي إلى الجانب الخلفي، و API إلى قاعدة البيانات، وتكوين إلى نشر، باستخدام الزخم الذي لا يتوقف لتقديم الميزات إلى الانتهاء، واستخدام بروتوكولات التكامل والنشر للنظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Building comprehensive systems that integrate frontend and backend functionalities","Implementing features that span multiple system boundaries, including API and database interactions","Creating and deploying complex configurations across different environments"],"zh":["构建集成前端和后端功能的综合系统","实现跨多个系统边界的功能，包括API和数据库交互","在不同环境中创建和部署复杂配置"],"ja":["フロントエンドとバックエンドの機能を統合した包括的なシステムを構築する","複数のシステム境界を越えた機能を実装する、APIやデータベースの相互作用を含む","さまざまな環境で複雑な構成を作成してデプロイする"],"ko":["전면과 후면 기능을 통합한 포괄적인 시스템을 구축하는 것","다수의 시스템 경계를越えた 기능을 구현하는 것, API 및 데이터베이스 상호 작용을 포함","다른 환경에서 복잡한 구성を作成하여 배포하는 것"],"es":["Construir sistemas integrales que integren funcionalidades de frontend y backend","Implementar características que abarcan múltiples fronteras de sistema, incluyendo interacciones de API y base de datos","Crear e implementar configuraciones complejas en diferentes entornos"],"fr":["Construire des systèmes complets qui intègrent des fonctionnalités de frontend et de backend","Mettre en œuvre des fonctionnalités qui s''étendent sur plusieurs frontières de système, y compris les interactions d''API et de base de données","Créer et déployer des configurations complexes dans différents environnements"],"de":["Umfassende Systeme aufbauen, die Frontend- und Backend-Funktionalitäten integrieren","Funktionen implementieren, die mehrere Systemgrenzen überschreiten, einschließlich API- und Datenbankinteraktionen","Komplexe Konfigurationen in verschiedenen Umgebungen erstellen und bereitstellen"],"pt":["Construir sistemas abrangentes que integrem funcionalidades de frontend e backend","Implementar recursos que abranjam múltiplas fronteiras do sistema, incluindo interações de API e banco de dados","Criar e implantar configurações complexas em diferentes ambientes"],"ru":["Построение комплексных систем, которые интегрируют функциональности frontend и backend","Реализация функций, охватывающих несколько границ системы, включая взаимодействия API и базы данных","Создание и развертывание сложных конфигураций в различных средах"],"ar":["بناء أنظمة شاملة تدمج وظائف الجانب الأمامي والجانب الخلفي","تنفيذ ميزات تتقاطع مع حدود متعددة للنظام، بما في ذلك التفاعلات مع API وقاعدة البيانات","إنشاء ونشر تكوينات معقدة في بيئات مختلفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear user requests to implement or build specific features or systems","May need additional tools or libraries for specific frontend, backend, API, or database functionalities"],"zh":["需要明确的用户请求来实现或构建特定的功能或系统","可能需要额外的工具或库来实现特定的前端、后端、API或数据库功能"],"ja":["特定の機能やシステムを実装または構築するために明確なユーザー要求が必要","特定のフロントエンド、バックエンド、APIまたはデータベースの機能を実現するために追加のツールまたはライブラリが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["특정 기능이나 시스템을 구현 또는 구축하기 위해 명확한 사용자 요청이 필요함","특정 전면, 후면, API 또는 데이터베이스 기능을 구현하기 위해 추가 도구 또는 라이브러리가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere solicitudes de usuario claras para implementar o construir características o sistemas específicos","Puede necesitar herramientas o bibliotecas adicionales para funcionalidades de frontend, backend, API o base de datos específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite des demandes d''utilisateur claires pour mettre en œuvre ou construire des fonctionnalités ou des systèmes spécifiques","Peut nécessiter des outils ou des bibliothèques supplémentaires pour des fonctionnalités de frontend, de backend, d''API ou de base de données spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt klare Benutzeranfragen, um bestimmte Funktionen oder Systeme zu implementieren oder zu erstellen","Benötigt möglicherweise zusätzliche Tools oder Bibliotheken für bestimmte Frontend-, Backend-, API- oder Datenbankfunktionalitäten"],"pt":["Exige solicitações de usuário claras para implementar ou construir recursos ou sistemas específicos","Pode precisar de ferramentas ou bibliotecas adicionais para funcionalidades específicas de frontend, backend, API ou banco de dados"],"ru":["Требует четких запросов пользователя для реализации или построения конкретных функций или систем","Может потребовать дополнительных инструментов или библиотек для конкретных функциональностей frontend, backend, API или базы данных"],"ar":["يتطلب طلبات مستخدم واضحة لتنفيذ أو بناء ميزات أو أنظمة محددة","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى أدوات أو مكتبات إضافية لميزات محددة من الجانب الأمامي والجانب الخلفي و API وقاعدة البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"02801f1a80fd63149061e5923ed18375f5d9f1c42d9270f34316f8c27b66f6ea","qualityScore":45}');
