ادات مساعد الترميز الذكي الشخصي","وكلاء متخصصون لتطوير بايثون ومل","السير العملية الآلية لتحسين الإنتاجية","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير مفتوحة المصدر","دعم بيئات متعددة للتطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理管理","Python开发工具","ML开发工具","AI编码助手","自动化工作流","CLI集成","Codex和Claude代码","如何使用AI智能代理管理","AI智能代理管理是什么","AI智能代理管理安装指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント管理","Python開発ツール","ML開発ツール","AIコーディングアシスタント","自動化ワークフロー","CLI統合","CodexとClaudeコード","AIエージェント管理の使い方","AIエージェント管理とは","AIエージェント管理のインストールガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 관리","파이썬 개발 도구","ML 개발 도구","AI 코딩 어시스턴트","자동화 워크플ロー","CLI 통합","Codex와 Claude 코드","AI 에이전트 관리 사용법","AI 에이전트 관리란","AI 에이전트 관리 설치 가이드"],"es":["agentes de IA para Python","herramientas de IA para ML","configuraciones de asistentes de codificación de IA","desarrollo de software con IA","automatización de tareas con IA","guias de instalación de agentes de IA","alternativas a los agentes de IA","cómo usar agentes de IA en el desarrollo de software","ventajas de los agentes de IA en el desarrollo de software"],"fr":["agents IA pour Python","outils IA pour ML","configurations d''assistants de codage IA","développement de logiciels avec IA","automatisation de tâches avec IA","guides d''installation d''agents IA","alternatives aux agents IA","comment utiliser des agents IA dans le développement de logiciels","avantages des agents IA dans le développement de logiciels"],"de":["AI-Agenten für Python","AI-Tools für ML","Konfigurationen für AI-Coding-Assistenten","Softwareentwicklung mit AI","Automatisierung von Aufgaben mit AI","Installationsanleitungen für AI-Agenten","Alternativen zu AI-Agenten","wie man AI-Agenten im Softwareentwicklung verwendet","Vorteile von AI-Agenten im Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["como usar agente de ia","o que é agente de ia","agente de ia para python","agente de ia para ml","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de ia","guias de instalação de agente de ia","alternativas de agente de ia"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент","что такое ИИ Агент","ИИ Агент для Python","ИИ Агент для ML","инструменты разработки ИИ","руководства по установке ИИ Агента","альтернативы ИИ Агента"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي","وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لبايثون","وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لمل","أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","دلائل تثبيت وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"Borda","repo":".home","repoPath":"Borda/.home","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T23:12:28Z","topics":["ai-agents","claude-agents","claude-code","claude-skills","codex","codex-agents","codex-cli"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"manage","description":"Create, update, or delete agents and skills with full cross-reference propagation across all .claude/ files and memory/MEMORY.md inventory.","bodyPreview":"<objective>\n\nManage the lifecycle of agents and skills in the `.claude/` directory. Handles creation with rich domain content, atomic updates (renames) with cross-reference propagation, and clean deletion with broken-reference cleanup. Keeps the MEMORY.md inventory in sync with what actually exists on disk.\n\n</objective>\n\n<inputs>\n\n- **$ARGUMENTS**: required, one of:\n  - `create agent <name> \"description\"` — create a new agent with generated domain content\n  - `create skill <name> \"description\"`","body":"<objective>\n\nManage the lifecycle of agents and skills in the `.claude/` directory. Handles creation with rich domain content, atomic updates (renames) with cross-reference propagation, and clean deletion with broken-reference cleanup. Keeps the MEMORY.md inventory in sync with what actually exists on disk.\n\n</objective>\n\n<inputs>\n\n- **$ARGUMENTS**: required, one of:\n  - `create agent <name> \"description\"` — create a new agent with generated domain content\n  - `create skill <name> \"description\"` — create a new skill with workflow scaffold\n  - `update agent <old-name> <new-name>` — rename agent file + update all cross-refs\n  - `update skill <old-name> <new-name>` — rename skill directory + update all cross-refs\n  - `delete agent <name>` — delete agent file + clean broken refs\n  - `delete skill <name>` — delete skill directory + clean broken refs\n- Names must be **kebab-case** (lowercase, hyphens only)\n- Descriptions must be quoted when they contain spaces\n\n**Agent examples:**\n\n- `/manage create agent security-auditor \"Security specialist for vulnerability scanning and OWASP compliance\"`\n- `/manage update agent ci-guardian ci-specialist`\n- `/manage delete agent old-agent-name`\n\n**Skill examples:**\n\n- `/manage create skill benchmark \"Benchmark orchestrator for measuring and comparing performance across commits\"`\n- `/manage update skill optimize perf-audit`\n- `/manage delete skill old-skill`\n\n</inputs>\n\n<constants>\n\n- AGENTS_DIR: `.claude/agents`\n- SKILLS_DIR: `.claude/skills`\n- MEMORY_FILE: `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/MEMORY.md`\n- USED_COLORS: blue, green, purple, lime, orange, yellow, cyan, red, teal, indigo, magenta, pink\n- AVAILABLE_COLORS: coral, gold, olive, navy, salmon, violet, maroon, aqua, brown\n\n</constants>\n\n<workflow>\n\n## Step 1: Parse and validate\n\nExtract operation, type, name, and optional arguments from `$ARGUMENTS`.\n\n**Validation rules:**\n\n- Name must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$` (kebab-case)\n- For `create`: name must NOT already exist on disk\n- For `update`/`delete`: name MUST already exist on disk\n- For `update`: new-name must NOT already exist on disk\n- For `create`: description is required\n\n```bash\n# Check existence\nls .claude/agents/<name>.md 2>/dev/null\nls .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nIf validation fails, report the error and stop.\n\n## Step 2: Overlap review (create only)\n\nBefore creating anything, check if existing agents/skills already cover the requested functionality:\n\n1. Read descriptions of all existing agents (`head -3` of each `.md` in agents/) and skills (`head -3` of each `SKILL.md`)\n2. Compare the new description against each existing one — look for domain overlap, similar workflows, or redundant scope\n3. Present findings to the user:\n   - **No overlap**: proceed to Step 3\n   - **Partial overlap**: name the overlapping agent/skill, explain what it covers vs what the new one would add, and ask the user whether to proceed, extend the existing one instead, or abort\n   - **Strong overlap**: recommend against creation — suggest using or extending the existing agent/skill instead\n\nSkip this step for `update` and `delete` operations.\n\n## Step 3: Inventory current state\n\nSnapshot the current roster for later comparison:\n\n```bash\n# Current agents\nls .claude/agents/*.md | xargs -n1 basename | sed ''s/\\.md$//'' | sort\n\n# Current skills\nls -d .claude/skills/*/ | xargs -n1 basename | sort\n\n# Colors in use\ngrep ''^color:'' .claude/agents/*.md\n```\n\n## Step 4: Execute operation\n\nBranch into one of six modes:\n\n### Mode: Create Agent\n\n1. Pick the first unused color from the AVAILABLE_COLORS pool (compare against colors found in Step 3)\n2. Choose model based on role complexity:\n   - `opusplan` — plan-gated roles (solution-architect, oss-maintainer, self-mentor): long-horizon reasoning + plan mode\n   - `opus` — complex implementation roles (sw-engineer, qa-specialist, ai-researcher, perf-optimizer): deep reasoning without plan mode\n   - `sonnet` — focused execution roles (linting-expert, data-steward, ci-guardian, web-explorer, doc-scribe): pattern-matching, structured output\n3. Write the agent file with real domain content derived from the description:\n\n**Agent template** — write to `AGENTS_DIR/<name>.md`:\n\n```\n---\nname / description / tools / model / color (frontmatter)\n---\n<role> — 2-3 sentences establishing expertise from description\n\\<core_knowledge> — 2 subsections, 3-5 bullets each (domain-specific, not generic)\n\n\\</core_knowledge>\n\n<workflow> — 5 numbered steps appropriate to the domain\n\n</workflow>\n\n\\<notes> — 1-2 operational notes + cross-refs to related agents\n\n\\</notes>\n\n```\n\n**Content rules:** `<role>` and `<workflow>` use normal tags; all other sections use `\\<escaped>` tags. Generate real domain content (80-120 lines total).\n\n### Mode: Create Skill\n\n1. Create the skill directory\n2. Write the skill file with workflow scaffold:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p .claude/skills/<name>\n```\n\n**Skill template** — write to `SKILLS_DIR/<name>/SKILL.md`:\n\n```\n---\nname / description / argument-hint / disable-model-invocation: true / allowed-tools (frontmatter)\n---\n<objective> — 2-3 sentences from description\n<inputs> — $ARGUMENTS documentation\n<workflow> — 3+ numbered steps with bash examples\n<notes> — operational caveats\n```\n\n**Content rules:** No backslash escaping in skills (all normal XML tags). Generate real steps (40-60 lines total). Default `allowed-tools` to `Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task` unless writing files is needed.\n\n### Mode: Update Agent\n\nAtomic update — write new file before deleting old:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Read the old file\ncat .claude/agents/<old-name>.md\n\n# 2. Write new file with updated name in frontmatter\n# (Edit the `name:` line in frontmatter to use new-name)\n\n# 3. Verify new file exists and is valid\nhead -5 .claude/agents/<new-name>.md\n\n# 4. Delete old file only after new file is confirmed\nrm .claude/agents/<old-name>.md\n```\n\n### Mode: Update Skill\n\nAtomic update — create new directory before removing old:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create new directory\nmkdir -p .claude/skills/<new-name>\n\n# 2. Copy SKILL.md with updated name in frontmatter\n# (Read old, edit name: line, write to new location)\n\n# 3. Verify new file exists\nhead -5 .claude/skills/<new-name>/SKILL.md\n\n# 4. Remove old directory only after new is confirmed\nrm -r .claude/skills/<old-name>\n```\n\n### Mode: Delete Agent\n\n```bash\n# Confirm existence before deleting\nls .claude/agents/<name>.md\nrm .claude/agents/<name>.md\n```\n\n### Mode: Delete Skill\n\n```bash\n# Confirm existence before deleting\nls .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md\nrm -r .claude/skills/<name>\n```\n\n## Step 5: Propagate cross-references\n\nSearch all `.claude/` markdown files for the changed name and update references:\n\n```bash\n# Find all references to the name across agents and skills\ngrep -rn \"<name>\" .claude/agents/*.md\ngrep -rn \"<name>\" .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\n```\n\n**For update:** Use the Edit tool to replace every occurrence of `<old-name>` with `<new-name>` in each file that references it.\n\n**For delete:** Review each reference. If the deleted name appears in:\n\n- A cross-reference suggestion (e.g., \"use X agent\") — remove or replace with the closest alternative\n- An inventory list — remove the entry\n- A workflow spawn directive — flag for manual review\n\n**For create:** No cross-ref propagation needed (new names have no existing references).\n\n## Step 6: Update memory/MEMORY.md\n\nRegenerate the inventory lines from what actually exists on disk:\n\n```bash\n# Get current agent list\nls .claude/agents/*.md | xargs -n1 basename | sed ''s/\\.md$//'' | paste -sd'', '' -\n\n# Get current skill list\nls -d .claude/skills/*/ | xargs -n1 basename | paste -sd'', '' -\n```\n\nUse the Edit tool to update these two lines in MEMORY.md:\n\n- `- Agents: oss-maintainer, sw-engineer, ...` (the roster line, not the path line)\n- `- Skills: review, security, ...`\n\n## Step 7: Update README.md\n\nUpdate the agent or skill table in `README.md`:\n\n- **create agent**: add a new row to the `### Agents` table — columns: `| **name** | Short tagline | Key capabilities |`\n- **create skill**: add a new row to the `### Skills` table — columns: `| **name** | \\`/name\\` | Description |\\`\n- **update (rename)**: find and replace the old name in the table row with the new name\n- **delete**: remove the row for the deleted name\n\nThe README tables are self-documenting — keep descriptions concise (one line) and consistent in tone with the surrounding rows. Do not add/remove table columns.\n\n## Step 8: Verify integrity\n\nConfirm no broken references remain:\n\n```bash\n# Extract all agent/skill names referenced in .claude/ files\ngrep -rohE ''[a-z]+-[a-z]+(-[a-z]+)*'' .claude/agents/*.md \\\n  .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md | sort -u\n\n# Compare against actual files on disk\nls .claude/agents/*.md | xargs -n1 basename | sed ''s/\\.md$//''\nls -d .claude/skills/*/ | xargs -n1 basename\n```\n\nUse Grep to search for the specific changed name and confirm:\n\n- **Update**: zero hits for old name, appropriate hits for new name\n- **Delete**: zero hits for deleted name (or flagged references noted)\n- **Create**: new file exists with valid structure\n\n## Step 9: Audit\n\nRun `/audit` to validate the created/modified file(s) and catch any issues introduced by this operation:\n\n```\n/audit\n```\n\nFor a targeted check of only the affected file, spawn **self-mentor** directly:\n\n- For `create`: audit the new file for structural completeness, cross-ref validity, and content quality\n- For `update`: audit the renamed file and verify no stale references remain\n- For `delete`: audit remaining files for broken references to the deleted name\n\nInclude the audit findings in the final report. Do not proceed to sync if any `critical` findings remain.\n\n## Step 10: Summary report\n\nOutput a structured report containing:\n\n- **Operation**: what was done (create/update/delete + type + name)\n- **Files Changed**: table of file paths and actions (created/renamed/deleted/cross-ref updated)\n- **Cross-References**: count of files updated, broken refs cleaned\n- **Current Roster**: agents (N) and skills (N) with comma-separated names\n- **Audit Result**: audit findings (pass / issues found)\n- **Follow-up**: run `/sync` to propagate to `~/.claude/`; for `create` review generated content; note if `settings.json` permissions might be needed\n\n</workflow>\n\n<notes>\n\n- **Atomic updates**: always write-before-delete to prevent data loss on interruption\n- **No settings.json auto-edit**: this skill only mentions when new permissions might be needed — it does not mutate JSON files to avoid risky structural edits\n- **README.md tables**: Step 7 updates the agent/skill tables in the project README.md — keep the row format consistent with existing rows\n- **Color pool**: the AVAILABLE_COLORS list provides unused colors for new agents; if exhausted, reuse colors with a note\n- **Cross-ref grep is broad**: searches bare kebab-case names across all markdown files — catches backtick references, prose mentions, spawn directives, and inventory lists\n- **MEMORY.md inventory**: always regenerated from disk (`ls`), never manually calculated — this prevents drift\n- Follow-up chains:\n  - After any create/update/delete → `/audit` to verify config integrity, then `/sync apply` to propagate\n  - After creating a new agent/skill → `/review` to validate generated content quality\n  - Recommended sequence: `/manage <op>` → `/audit` → `/sync apply`\n\n</notes>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T01:58:12.031Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, or LangChain requiring streamlined lifecycle management of agents and skills within the .claude/ directory.","zh":"适用于 Claude、AutoGPT 或 LangChain 等 AI Agent，需要在 .claude/ 目录中对 Agent 和技能进行流线化的生命周期管理。","ja":"Claude、AutoGPT、または LangChain などの AI エージェントに適しています。これらは、.claude/ ディレクトリ内でのエージェントとスキルのストリームライン化されたライフサイクル管理を必要とします。","ko":"Claude, AutoGPT 또는 LangChain과 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 이러한 에이전트는 .claude/ 디렉토리 내에서 에이전트 및 스킬의 스트림라인화된 生命周期 관리를 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT o LangChain que requieren una gestión de ciclo de vida optimizada de agentes y habilidades dentro del directorio .claude/","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude, AutoGPT ou LangChain nécessitant une gestion de cycle de vie rationalisée des agents et des compétences au sein du répertoire .claude/","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude, AutoGPT oder LangChain, die eine optimierte Lebenszyklusverwaltung von Agents und Fähigkeiten innerhalb des Verzeichnisses .claude/ erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT ou LangChain que exigem gerenciamento de ciclo de vida simplificado de agentes e habilidades dentro do diretório .claude/","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, AutoGPT или LangChain, требующих упрощенного управления жизненным циклом агентов и навыков внутри директории .claude/","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude، AutoGPT أو LangChain الذي يتطلب إدارة دورة حياة مبسطة للوكلاء والمهارات داخل 目录 .claude/"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to efficiently create, update, and delete configurations with rich domain content, leveraging atomic updates and cross-reference propagation, while maintaining a synchronized MEMORY.md inventory using Python and ML open-source development tools.","zh":"赋予代理人使用 Python 和 ML 开源开发工具，利用原子更新和跨引用传播，高效地创建、更新和删除配置，并保持 MEMORY.md 清单的同步。","ja":"Python と ML のオープンソース開発ツールを使用して、エージェントに原子更新とクロスリファレンス伝播を活用し、構成を効率的に作成、更新、削除し、MEMORY.md のインベントリを同期させます。","ko":"파이썬과 ML 오픈소스 개발 도구를 사용하여 에이전트가 원자적 업데이트와 크로스 참조 전파를 활용하여 구성의 효율적인 생성, 업데이트 및 삭제를 가능하게 하며, MEMORY.md 인벤토리의 동기화를 유지합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear, actualizar y eliminar configuraciones de manera eficiente con contenido de dominio rico, aprovechando actualizaciones atómicas y propagación de referencias cruzadas, mientras mantiene un inventario MEMORY.md sincronizado utilizando herramientas de desarrollo de código abierto Python y ML.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer, de mettre à jour et de supprimer des configurations de manière efficace avec un contenu de domaine riche, en exploitant les mises à jour atomiques et la propagation des références croisées, tout en maintenant un inventaire MEMORY.md synchronisé en utilisant des outils de développement open-source Python et ML.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Konfigurationen effizient zu erstellen, zu aktualisieren und zu löschen, mit reichem Domäneninhalt, der atomare Updates und Kreuzreferenz-Propagierung nutzt, während ein synchronisierter MEMORY.md-Bestand mithilfe von Python- und ML-Open-Source-Entwicklungstools aufrechterhalten wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem, atualizem e excluam configurações de forma eficiente com conteúdo de domínio rico, aproveitando atualizações atômicas e propagação de referências cruzadas, mantendo um inventário MEMORY.md sincronizado usando ferramentas de desenvolvimento de código aberto Python e ML","ru":"Позволяет агентам эффективно создавать, обновлять и удалять конфигурации с богатым доменным контентом, используя атомарные обновления и распространение перекрестных ссылок, при этом поддерживая синхронизированный инвентарь MEMORY.md с помощью инструментов разработки с открытым исходным кодом Python и ML","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء وتحديث وحذف التكوينات بفعالية مع محتوى نطاق غني، مستفيدة من التحديثات الذرية وانتشار المراجع المتقاطعة، مع الحفاظ على مخزون MEMORY.md متزامن باستخدام أدوات تطوير مفتوحة المصدر Python و ML"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new agents with generated domain content","Updating existing skills with automated cross-reference propagation","Cleaning up deleted configurations with broken-reference cleanup"],"zh":["创建具有生成的领域内容的新代理人","使用自动化的跨引用传播更新现有的技能","使用断开的引用清理清除已删除的配置"],"ja":["生成されたドメインコンテンツを持つ新しいエージェントを作成する","自動化されたクロスリファレンス伝播を使用して既存のスキルを更新する","切断された参照のクリーンアップを使用して削除された構成をクリーンアップする"],"ko":["생성된 도메인 콘텐츠를 가지는 새로운 에이전트를 생성합니다","자동화된 크로스 참조 전파를 사용하여 기존의 스킬을 업데이트합니다","끊어진 참조의 정리를 사용하여 삭제된 구성의 정리"],"es":["Crear nuevos agentes con contenido de dominio generado","Actualizar habilidades existentes con propagación automática de referencias cruzadas","Limpiar configuraciones eliminadas con limpieza de referencias rotas"],"fr":["Créer de nouveaux agents avec un contenu de domaine généré","Mettre à jour des compétences existantes avec une propagation automatique de références croisées","Nettoyer les configurations supprimées avec un nettoyage de références cassées"],"de":["Erstellen neuer Agents mit generiertem Domäneninhalt","Aktualisieren bestehender Fähigkeiten mit automatischer Kreuzreferenz-Propagierung","Bereinigen gelöschter Konfigurationen mit Bereinigung von fehlerhaften Referenzen"],"pt":["Criar novos agentes com conteúdo de domínio gerado","Atualizar habilidades existentes com propagação de referências cruzadas automatizada","Limpar configurações excluídas com limpeza de referências quebradas"],"ru":["Создание новых агентов с сгенерированным доменным контентом","Обновление существующих навыков с автоматическим распространением перекрестных ссылок","Очистка удаленных конфигураций с очисткой сломанных ссылок"],"ar":["إنشاء وكلاء جدد مع محتوى نطاق تم إنشاؤه","تحديث مهارات موجودة مع انتشار مراجع متقاطعة تلقائي","تنظيف التكوينات المحذوفة مع تنظيف المراجع المكسورة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the .claude/ directory","Limited to Python and ML open-source development","Needs MEMORY.md inventory for synchronization"],"zh":["需要访问 .claude/ 目录","仅限于 Python 和 ML 开源开发","需要 MEMORY.md 清单来实现同步"],"ja":[".claude/ ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","Python と ML のオープンソース開発に限定される","同期のために MEMORY.md のインベントリが必要"],"ko":[".claude/ 디렉토리에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","파이썬과 ML 오픈소스 개발에만 제한됩니다","동기화를 위해 MEMORY.md 인벤토리가 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio .claude/","Limitado a desarrollo de código abierto Python y ML","Necesita un inventario MEMORY.md para la sincronización"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au répertoire .claude/","Limité au développement open-source Python et ML","Nécessite un inventaire MEMORY.md pour la synchronisation"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis .claude/","Begrenzt auf Open-Source-Entwicklung mit Python und ML","Benötigt einen MEMORY.md-Bestand für die Synchronisierung"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao diretório .claude/","Limitado a desenvolvimento de código aberto Python e ML","Necessita de inventário MEMORY.md para sincronização"],"ru":["Требует доступа к директории .claude/","Ограничен разработкой с открытым исходным кодом Python и ML","Требует инвентаря MEMORY.md для синхронизации"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الدليل .claude/","محدود بالتطوير مفتوح المصدر Python و ML","يحتاج إلى مخزون MEMORY.md للتنسيق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"9f0006f35098bcaf51aee51f7eb01296e8da360651acdc5c86a44f6378dccc44","qualityScore":45}');
