템 및 애플리케이션에 대응","다양한 프로그래밍 언어 및 개발 프레임워크를 지원","詳細한 문서 및 샘플 코드를 제공"],"es":["Marco de evaluación para agentes de telemetría","Integración con inteligencia artificial","Análisis de datos en tiempo real","Mejora de la eficiencia de los proyectos","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas"],"fr":["Cadre d''évaluation pour les agents de télémétrie","Intégration avec l''intelligence artificielle","Analyse de données en temps réel","Amélioration de l''efficacité des projets","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plates-formes"],"de":["Bewertungsframework für Telemetrie-Agenten","Integration mit künstlicher Intelligenz","Echtzeit-Datenanalyse","Verbesserung der Effizienz von Projekten","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen"],"pt":["Estrutura de pesquisa e avaliação para agentes de instrumentação de telemetria com IA","Integração com React, Python, Node.js e CLI","Suporte a agentes de telemetria para coletar dados de desempenho","Análise de dados em tempo real com IA","Relatórios personalizados para visualização de dados"],"ru":["Исследовательская и оценочная база для ИИ агентов телеметрической инструментации","Интеграция с React, Python, Node.js и CLI","Поддержка агентов телеметрии для сбора данных о производительности","Анализ данных в реальном времени с ИИ","Пользовательские отчеты для визуализации данных"],"ar":["إطار بحث وتقييم للوكلاء仪ات تليميتيا الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع React، Python، Node.js و CLI","دعم وكلاء التليميتيا لجمع بيانات الأداء","تحليل البيانات في الوقت الفعلي بالذكاء الاصطناعي","تقارير مخصصة لتصور البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能体","遥测仪表化代理","prd-phase框架","AI系统优化","如何使用prd-phase","prd-phase教程","AI智能体开发","遥测仪表化代理研究","AI系统评估"],"ja":["AIエージェント","テレメトリーシステム","prd-phaseフレームワーク","AIシステム最適化","prd-phaseの使い方","prd-phaseチュートリアル","AIエージェント開発","テレメトリーシステム研究","AIシステム評価"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","원격 측정 시스템","prd-phase 프레임워크","AI 시스템 최적화","prd-phase 사용법","prd-phase 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트 개발","원격 측정 시스템 연구","AI 시스템 평가"],"es":["cómo usar prd-phase","qué es un agente de telemetría AI","prd-phase alternativa","prd-phase vs New Relic","instalación de prd-phase","guía de configuración de prd-phase"],"fr":["comment utiliser prd-phase","qu''est-ce qu''un agent de télémétrie IA","alternative à prd-phase","prd-phase vs New Relic","installation de prd-phase","guide de configuration de prd-phase"],"de":["wie man prd-phase verwendet","was ist ein AI-Telemetrie-Agent","Alternative zu prd-phase","prd-phase vs New Relic","Installation von prd-phase","Konfigurationsanleitung für prd-phase"],"pt":["como usar prd-phase","o que é prd-phase","alternativas para prd-phase","prd-phase vs new relic","instalar prd-phase","guia de configuração do prd-phase","desenvolvimento de agentes de telemetria com IA","integração de prd-phase com React","prd-phase e Python"],"ru":["как использовать prd-phase","что такое prd-phase","альтернативы prd-phase","prd-phase vs new relic","установка prd-phase","руководство по настройке prd-phase","разработка агентов телеметрии с ИИ","интеграция prd-phase с React","prd-phase и Python"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام prd-phase","ما هو prd-phase","بديلات ل prd-phase","prd-phase مقابل new relic","تثبيت prd-phase","دليل إعداد prd-phase","تطوير وكلاء التليميتيا بالذكاء الاصطناعي","تكامل prd-phase مع React","prd-phase و Python"]}},"owner":"wiggitywhitney","repo":"telemetry-agent-research","repoPath":"wiggitywhitney/telemetry-agent-research","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T10:17:42Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd-phase","description":"Create implementation phase PRDs from pre-existing research for the telemetry agent. Translates already-complete research into focused, bounded PRDs. Use when the user says prd-phase N or wants to create a PRD for a specific build phase (1-7). Do NOT use for new feature discovery — use prd-create for that.","bodyPreview":"# Phase PRD Creation\n\n## Purpose\n\nCreate implementation phase PRDs for the telemetry agent by assembling content from existing research documents. All research is complete. The job is to route to the right documents, extract the right details, and produce a focused PRD.\n\n## Critical Principles\n\n1. **Bounded context**: Read ONLY what this phase needs. Do not read the full spec or full tech stack document. Read the specific sections listed in the routing tables below.\n2. **No detail loss**: Versio","body":"# Phase PRD Creation\n\n## Purpose\n\nCreate implementation phase PRDs for the telemetry agent by assembling content from existing research documents. All research is complete. The job is to route to the right documents, extract the right details, and produce a focused PRD.\n\n## Critical Principles\n\n1. **Bounded context**: Read ONLY what this phase needs. Do not read the full spec or full tech stack document. Read the specific sections listed in the routing tables below.\n2. **No detail loss**: Version numbers, API patterns, config field names, and code snippets must be copied verbatim from source documents into the PRD. Do not summarize technical details.\n3. **Excerpt, don''t just reference**: Critical details (acceptance gates, API patterns, rubric rules) must be IN the PRD, not just referenced by section name.\n4. **One phase at a time**: Never create multiple phase PRDs in one session. Each phase gets a fresh context.\n5. **JavaScript and ESM**: The agent is JavaScript (`\"type\": \"module\"` in package.json). All code samples use ESM `import` syntax. ts-morph is used for AST analysis (it handles JS via `allowJs: true`), but the agent code itself is JavaScript.\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Phase\n\nParse the phase number (1-7) from the user''s command.\n\n### Step 2: Read the Phase Definition\n\nRead the specific phase section from `docs/specs/research/implementation-phasing.md`. Each phase contains:\n- What Gets Built\n- Acceptance Gate\n- Rubric Rules That Apply\n- Why This Boundary\n- Spec Sections (table mapping to spec sections and subsections)\n\n**Also read these cross-cutting sections** (they apply to every phase):\n- \"Two-Tier Validation Architecture\" section\n- \"Cross-Cutting: The DX Principle\" section\n\n### Step 3: Read Source Documents (Routing)\n\nRead ONLY the sections relevant to this phase.\n\n#### 3a. Spec Sections\n\nThe phase definition contains a \"Spec Sections\" table. For each row:\n- **Full** -> read the entire section from `docs/specs/telemetry-agent-spec-v3.8.md`\n- **Subsection only** -> read only the named subsection\n- **Fields only** -> extract just the named configuration fields\n- **Row only** -> extract just the named row from the Technology Stack table\n\n**Note**: The spec was renamed from v3.5.md → v3.6.md → v3.7.md → v3.8.md as content versions evolved.\n\n**Spec section landmarks** (line numbers for the 1,796-line spec):\n\n| Section | Line | Key Subsections |\n|---------|------|-----------------|\n| Architecture | 54 | Coordinator+Agents 56, Coordinator API 131, Error Handling 163, Interfaces 196, Tech Stack 223, Weaver Integration 256 |\n| Init Phase (Required) | 293 | What Init Does 297, Prerequisites 327 |\n| Complete Workflow | 337 | (diagram through ~400) |\n| How It Works | 400 | Input 402, Processing (per file) 407, Output 423, Agent Output Format 427, System Prompt Structure 441, Known Failure Modes 471, Elision Detection 487 |\n| File/Directory Processing | 497 | File Revert Protocol 509, Periodic Schema Checkpoints 515 |\n| What Gets Instrumented | 531 | Priority Hierarchy 533, Review Sensitivity 546, Patterns Not Covered 563 |\n| What the Agent Actually Does to Code | 576 | Path 1: Auto-Instrumentation 580, Path 2: Manual Span 650, Decision: Which Path? 714 |\n| Attribute Priority Chain | 724 | Schema Extension Guardrails 734 |\n| Auto-Instrumentation Libraries | 748 | Why Libraries First 752, Detection Flow 758, Library Discovery 777 |\n| Validation Chain | 877 | Per-File Validation (with fix loop) 881, End-of-Run Validation 987 |\n| Agent Self-Instrumentation | 1024 | |\n| Handling Existing Instrumentation | 1083 | |\n| Schema as Source of Truth | 1101 | |\n| Result Data | 1110 | Result Structure 1120, PR Summary 1246, Schema Hash Tracking 1260 |\n| Configuration | 1266 | What Goes Where 1317, Dependency Strategy 1357, Cost Visibility 1372 |\n| Minimum Viable Schema Example | 1386 | |\n| PoC Scope | 1582 | In Scope 1584, Out of Scope 1631 |\n| Evaluation & Acceptance Criteria | 1647 | Two-Tier Validation Architecture 1681, Required Verification Levels 1715 |\n\n#### 3b. Tech Stack Sections\n\nRead `references/tech-stack-by-phase.md` (bundled with this skill) to find which sections of `docs/architecture/tech-stack-evaluation.md` to read for this phase. Extract:\n- Version numbers (exact)\n- API patterns (code snippets, verbatim)\n- Caveats and limitations\n- Recommendation summaries\n\n#### 3c. Rubric Rules\n\nThe phase definition lists rubric rule IDs (e.g., NDS-001, CDQ-003). Look up each rule''s full definition in `research/evaluation-rubric.md`. The code-level rules are in **Part 2: Code-Level Evaluation** (line 136), organized as:\n\n| Dimension | Location | Rules |\n|-----------|----------|-------|\n| Gate Checks | ~line 140 | NDS-001, NDS-002, NDS-003, API-001 |\n| Non-Destructiveness | ~line 189 | NDS-004, NDS-005 |\n| Coverage | ~line 218 | COV-001 through COV-006 |\n| Restraint | ~line 282 | RST-001 through RST-005 |\n| API-Only Dependency | ~line 337 | API-002, API-003, API-004 |\n| Schema Fidelity | ~line 374 | SCH-001 through SCH-004 |\n| Code Quality | ~line 422 | CDQ-001 through CDQ-008 |\n\nFor each rule, extract: Rule ID, name, impact level, evaluation scope, full description including evaluation method, and automation classification (summary at ~line 514).\n\nFor Phase 2+, classify rules as Tier 1 (structural/blocking) vs Tier 2 (semantic/blocking or advisory) using the \"Two-Tier Validation Architecture\" section of implementation-phasing.md.\n\n#### 3d. Architectural Context (if needed)\n\nRead relevant sections of `docs/architecture/recommendations.md`:\n- Phases 1-3: \"Fix Loop Feedback Quality\" subsection\n- Phase 2: \"Two-Tier Validation (New Architecture)\" section\n- Phases 4-7: \"DX and Error Handling Architecture\" section\n- All phases: Summary table at end for quick reference\n\n### Step 4: Assemble the PRD\n\nRead `references/phase-prd-template.md` (bundled with this skill) for the output template.\n\nFill in each section using content gathered in Steps 2-3. Key rules:\n\n**Tech Stack section:**\n- Copy version numbers exactly (e.g., \"Vitest 4.0.18\", not \"latest\")\n- Copy API code snippets verbatim — all JavaScript, ESM imports\n- Include caveats that affect THIS phase\n- Include only entries relevant to this phase\n\n**Rubric Rules section:**\n- Include the full rule definition, not just the ID\n- Group by Gate vs Dimension\n- Note which are Tier 1 vs Tier 2 (for Phase 2+)\n- Include impact level and automation classification\n\n**Acceptance Gate section:**\n- Copy the gate verbatim from the phasing document\n- Add specific, testable verification steps\n- Map each gate criterion to the rubric rules that verify it\n\n**Milestones:**\n- Define 5-8 milestones that build toward the acceptance gate incrementally\n- Each milestone should be independently testable\n- Final milestone: \"Acceptance gate passes end-to-end\"\n- Include a milestone for the DX cross-cutting requirement specific to this phase\n\n**Spec Reference section:**\n- Reproduce the spec section map table from the phasing document\n- Add line number ranges from the landmarks table above\n\n### Step 5: Create GitHub Issue and PRD File\n\nFollow the same workflow as `/prd-create`:\n\n1. **Create GitHub Issue** with label \"PRD\":\n   ```markdown\n   ## PRD: Phase N — [Phase Name]\n\n   **Problem**: Implementation phase N of the telemetry agent — [what gets built]\n\n   **Solution**: [1-2 sentence summary from phasing document]\n\n   **Detailed PRD**: Will be added after PRD file creation\n\n   **Priority**: High\n   ```\n\n2. **Create PRD file** at `prds/[issue-id]-phase-N-[phase-name].md`\n\n3. **Update GitHub Issue** with PRD link\n\n4. **Commit** with `[skip ci]` flag:\n   ```text\n   docs(prd-[issue-id]): create Phase N PRD — [phase-name] [skip ci]\n   ```\n\n### Step 6: Post-Creation Verification\n\nBefore presenting the PRD to the user, verify:\n\n- [ ] Every rubric rule ID listed in the phasing document appears with its full definition\n- [ ] Every spec section from the phase''s spec section map is referenced with line numbers\n- [ ] Tech stack version numbers are exact (not \"latest\" or \"current\")\n- [ ] API code snippets are present and use JavaScript ESM syntax\n- [ ] The acceptance gate is copied verbatim from the phasing document\n- [ ] The DX cross-cutting requirement for this phase is included\n- [ ] No content from other phases leaked in\n- [ ] Milestones build incrementally toward the acceptance gate\n- [ ] All code samples are JavaScript (not TypeScript)\n\n## Source Documents\n\n| Document | Path | Purpose |\n|----------|------|---------|\n| Implementation Phasing | `docs/specs/research/implementation-phasing.md` | Phase definitions, spec section maps, cross-cutting architecture |\n| Telemetry Agent Spec | `docs/specs/telemetry-agent-spec-v3.8.md` | Source of truth for what to build |\n| Tech Stack Evaluation | `docs/architecture/tech-stack-evaluation.md` | Version numbers, API patterns, library choices |\n| Evaluation Rubric | `research/evaluation-rubric.md` | Full rule definitions for acceptance criteria |\n| Architectural Recommendations | `docs/architecture/recommendations.md` | Preserve/change verdicts, evidence base |\n| Tech Stack by Phase | `references/tech-stack-by-phase.md` (skill-bundled) | Routing table: which tech stack sections per phase |\n| Phase PRD Template | `references/phase-prd-template.md` (skill-bundled) | Output template |\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **One phase per session.** Multiple phase PRDs in one context risks detail loss.\n- **The spec is the source of truth.** If the phasing document and spec disagree, the spec wins. Flag the discrepancy for the user.\n- **Don''t include evaluation findings.** The implementing AI needs what to build, not why the last attempt failed.\n- **Don''t include rejected alternatives.** No LangGraph comparisons, no Babel evaluations.\n- **Trust the routing tables.** Don''t add \"extra context that might be helpful.\"\n- **JavaScript only.** The agent code is JavaScript with ESM modules. ts-morph handles JS via `allowJs: true`. All samples, all paths, all config — JavaScript.\n\n**Note**: If any `gh` command fails with \"command not found\", inform the user that GitHub CLI is required: https://cli.github.com/\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T03:24:09.310Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing structured content analysis for PRD creation","zh":"非常适合需要结构化内容分析以创建 PRD 的技术写作代理","ja":"技術文章作成エージェントが構造化されたコンテンツ分析を必要とする PRD 作成に最適","ko":"구조화된 콘텐츠 분석이 필요한 기술 문서 에이전트를 위한 PRD 생성에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Escritura Técnica que necesitan análisis de contenido estructurado para la creación de PRD","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de rédaction technique nécessitant une analyse de contenu structurée pour la création de PRD","de":"Perfekt für technische Schreibagenten, die eine strukturierte Inhaltsanalyse für die PRD-Erstellung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Redação Técnica que necessitam de análise de conteúdo estruturada para criação de PRD","ru":"Идеально для Технических Агентов по Написанию, которым требуется структурированный анализ контента для создания PRD","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النصوص التقنية الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل محتوى منظم لإنشاء PRD"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to assemble focused PRDs by extracting relevant details from existing research documents, utilizing routing tables and bounded context principles to ensure no detail loss, all while working within specific sections of tech stack documents","zh":"赋予代理人通过从现有研究文档中提取相关细节、利用路由表和有界上下文原则以确保不丢失细节，同时在技术栈文档的特定部分内工作，从而组装出重点的 PRD 的能力","ja":"ルーティングテーブルと境界付きコンテキスト原則を使用して、既存の研究文書から関連する詳細を抽出し、技術スタック文書の特定のセクション内で作業することで、詳細の損失なく焦点を当てた PRD を作成するエージェントの能力を付与する","ko":"기존 연구 문서에서 관련 세부 정보를 추출하고, 라우팅 테이블 및 경계 컨텍스트 원칙을 사용하여 세부 정보가 손실되지 않도록 하며, 기술 스택 문서의 특정 섹션에서 작업하여 집중적인 PRD를 조립할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ensamblar PRD enfocados extrayendo detalles relevantes de documentos de investigación existentes, utilizando tablas de enrutamiento y principios de contexto acotado para garantizar que no se pierdan detalles, todo mientras se trabaja dentro de secciones específicas de documentos de pila tecnológica","fr":"Permet aux agents d''assembler des PRD ciblés en extrayant des détails pertinents de documents de recherche existants, en utilisant des tables de routage et des principes de contexte borné pour garantir qu''aucun détail ne soit perdu, le tout en travaillant dans des sections spécifiques de documents de pile technologique","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, fokussierte PRD zu erstellen, indem sie relevante Details aus bestehenden Forschungsdokumenten extrahieren, Routing-Tabellen und Prinzipien des beschränkten Kontexts verwenden, um sicherzustellen, dass keine Details verloren gehen, während sie innerhalb bestimmter Abschnitte von Technologie-Stack-Dokumenten arbeiten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a montar PRDs focados, extrair detalhes relevantes de documentos de pesquisa existentes, utilizando tabelas de roteamento e princípios de contexto limitado para garantir que nenhum detalhe seja perdido, tudo isso trabalhando dentro de seções específicas de documentos de pilha de tecnologia","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью собирать сосредоточенные PRD, извлекая соответствующие детали из существующих исследовательских документов, используя маршрутизационные таблицы и принципы ограниченного контекста, чтобы гарантировать, что не будет потеряно ни одна деталь, все это при работе в определенных разделах документов технологического стека","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تجميع PRDs متعمقة من خلال استخراج التفاصيل ذات الصلة من وثائق البحث الموجودة، باستخدام جداول التوجيه ومبادئ السياق المحدود لضمان عدم فقدان أي تفاصيل، مع العمل داخل أقسام محددة من وثائق المكدس التقني"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating PRD creation for telemetry instrumentation agents","Generating implementation phase documents from research findings","Extracting critical details from technical specifications"],"zh":["为遥测仪器代理创建 PRD 的自动化","从研究结果生成实施阶段文档","从技术规格中提取关键细节"],"ja":["テレメトリインストルメンテーションエージェントの PRD 作成の自動化","研究結果から実装段階のドキュメントを生成する","技術仕様から重要な詳細を抽出する"],"ko":["계측 에이전트를 위한 PRD 생성 자동화","연구 결과에서 구현 단계 문서 생성","기술 사양에서 중요한 세부 정보 추출"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de PRD para agentes de instrumentación de telemetría","Generación de documentos de fase de implementación a partir de resultados de investigación","Extracción de detalles críticos de especificaciones técnicas"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de PRD pour les agents d''instrumentation de télémétrie","Génération de documents de phase d''implémentation à partir de résultats de recherche","Extraction de détails critiques de spécifications techniques"],"de":["Automatisierung der PRD-Erstellung für Telemetrie-Instrumentierungsagenten","Erstellung von Implementierungsphasendokumenten aus Forschungsergebnissen","Extraktion kritischer Details aus technischen Spezifikationen"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de PRD para agentes de instrumentação de telemetria","Gerar documentos de fase de implementação a partir de descobertas de pesquisa","Extrair detalhes críticos de especificações técnicas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание PRD для агентов телметрической инструментовки","Генерировать документы фазы реализации из результатов исследований","Извлекать критические детали из технических спецификаций"],"ar":["تحويل processo من إنشاء PRD إلى تلقائي لوكلاء أدوات التелеметري","توليد وثائق مرحلة التنفيذ من نتائج البحث","استخراج التفاصيل الحرجة من المواصفات الفنية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing research documents and routing tables","Bounded context must be strictly followed to avoid detail loss"],"zh":["需要现有的研究文档和路由表","必须严格遵循有界上下文以避免细节丢失"],"ja":["既存の研究文書とルーティングテーブルが必要","詳細の損失を避けるために、境界付きコンテキストに厳密に従う必要がある"],"ko":["既存의 연구 문서와 라우팅 테이블이 필요","세부 정보가 손실되지 않도록 경계 컨텍스트를 엄격히 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere documentos de investigación existentes y tablas de enrutamiento","El contexto acotado debe seguirse estrictamente para evitar la pérdida de detalles"],"fr":["Nécessite des documents de recherche existants et des tables de routage","Le contexte borné doit être suivi strictement pour éviter la perte de détails"],"de":["Benötigt bestehende Forschungsdokumente und Routing-Tabellen","Der beschränkte Kontext muss streng eingehalten werden, um den Verlust von Details zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Requer documentos de pesquisa existentes e tabelas de roteamento","O contexto limitado deve ser estritamente seguido para evitar perda de detalhes"],"ru":["Требует существующих исследовательских документов и маршрутизационных таблиц","Ограниченный контекст должен быть строго соблюдён, чтобы избежать потери деталей"],"ar":["يتطلب وثائق بحث موجودة وجداول توجيه","يجب اتباع السياق المحدود严格 لتفادي فقدان التفاصيل"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3066121544454be4a9b5c05b82e301e221f10ef6f910e4f1b5a176bb962d28a0","qualityScore":45}');
